(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:`${w}.q${i+1}`,senseId:`${w}.s${q.s}`,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('source','Source came through Old French sourse, “a spring or fountain,” from Latin surgere, “to rise”; its meanings extend from an origin to a person or place that supplies something.',[C('source.s1','research','The archivist named the interview as her source and linked the recording in the report.','档案员把这次访谈列为资料来源，并在报告中附上录音链接。','cite/name a source; source for a claim','名词指提供信息或物品的人、书籍或地点。','The cited interview supplies information for the report.','被引用的访谈为报告提供信息。'),C('source.s2','geography','We followed the stream uphill until we reached its source beneath a rocky ledge.','我们沿小溪向上走，直到找到岩架下的源头。','the source of a river/problem','名词也指河流或问题开始的地方。','The stream begins at this point.','小溪从这个地点发源。'),C('source.s3','business','The studio sources its wool from farms that publish animal-welfare audits.','这家工作室从公开动物福利审查结果的农场采购羊毛。','source materials/products from a supplier','动词作及物用法，表示从某地或某人取得供应品。','The farms are where the studio obtains the wool.','这些农场是工作室获取羊毛的地方。')],M('The editor sourced the figures from a report that did not contain them and had never been consulted.','The editor sourced the figures from the report that actually published them.','来源必须实际提供所引用的信息，不能是未包含数据的报告。','word-choice'),[Q(1,'What is the interview in the archivist’s report?','the material that provides information','the place where a river begins','a supplier of wool','A source can be a person or document that supplies information.'),Q(2,'Where is the stream’s source?','where it begins beneath the ledge','where it enters the sea','where the archivist stores recordings','The geographic sense means the starting point of a river.'),Q(3,'What does the studio do with its wool?','obtains it from audited farms','publishes a river map','cites it as a newspaper article','To source a product is to obtain it from a supplier.'),Q(3,'Which construction is natural?','source wool from local farms','source wool into a local farm','source wool at a report','The verb commonly takes the product as object and uses “from” for its supplier.','collocation')]);
P('sourness','Sourness is formed from sour + -ness; the suffix turns the adjective into a noun for the quality or state of being sour.',[C('sourness.s1','food','A little lemon juice added sourness to the lentil soup and balanced its sweetness.','加了一点柠檬汁后，扁豆汤有了酸味，也平衡了甜味。','the sourness of lemon; add sourness to','名词指柠檬或醋那样尖锐的酸味。','The soup tastes sharply acidic after the lemon is added.','加入柠檬后汤有明显酸味。'),C('sourness.s2','food safety','The sourness and smell of the milk suggested that it had spoiled overnight.','牛奶的酸味和气味表明它在夜里变质了。','a smell/taste of sourness','名词也可指食物变质后发酸的状态。','The milk has turned unpleasantly sour rather than being freshly acidic.','牛奶变成令人不快的馊酸味，而非新鲜酸味。')],M('The sourness of the spoiled milk proved it was fresh, sweet, and safe to drink.','The sourness of the milk warned us that it had spoiled.','变质牛奶的酸馊味是食物变质的迹象，不说明它新鲜安全。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did lemon juice add to the soup?','a sharp acidic taste','a smell of spoiled milk','a handful of lentils','Sourness sense 1 is a sharp taste like lemon or vinegar.'),Q(2,'Why did the milk seem unsafe?','it had an unpleasant sour taste and smell','it tasted fresh and sweet','it was served with lemon','The second sense describes food that has gone bad.'),Q(1,'How is sourness formed?','sour plus the noun-forming suffix -ness','sour plus the verb ending -ed','south plus -ern','-ness names a quality or state.'),Q(2,'Which clue points to spoilage rather than a recipe’s acidity?','milk developing an off smell overnight','lemon brightening a soup','vinegar being added deliberately','The spoilage sense includes food turning unpleasantly sour.')]);
P('south','South is from Old English sūþ, a Germanic direction word; it can name the direction or region, modify a place, or indicate movement toward it.',[C('south.s1','geography','The hikers turned south at the stone bridge and followed the river toward the coast.','徒步者在石桥处转向南，沿河朝海岸走去。','turn/go to the south; south of town','名词指与北相反的方向或一个地区的南部。','The bridge marks the point where their route changes direction.','石桥是路线改变方向的地点。'),C('south.s2','weather','A south wind brought warm, humid air across the valley before the storm.','暴风雨来临前，一股南风把温暖潮湿的空气吹过山谷。','a south wind; south-facing slope','形容词表示位于南方、朝南或来自南方。','The wind comes from the southern direction.','风来自南方。'),C('south.s3','travel','The train continued south after leaving the central station.','列车离开中央车站后继续向南行驶。','travel/head south','副词说明向南移动。','South modifies the direction of continued travel.','south 修饰继续行进的方向。')],M('After the bridge the hikers went south, directly toward the northern border.','After the bridge the hikers went south, toward the coast.','南向路线不能同时指向相反的北方边界。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Where did the hikers turn?','toward the south','toward the north','toward the valley floor only','South names the direction opposite north.'),Q(2,'Where does a south wind come from?','from the south','from the north','from below the ground','A south wind is named for the direction it comes from.'),Q(3,'What did the train do after the station?','continued toward the south','turned into a south-facing room','began blowing warm air','Here south is an adverb of direction.'),Q(2,'In “a south-facing slope,” south functions as…','an adjective describing orientation','a verb meaning turn','a noun meaning weather','It modifies the noun slope.')]);
P('southeast','Southeast combines south and east for the compass direction midway between them, and for places or movement in that direction.',[C('southeast.s1','navigation','From the campsite, the river bends southeast toward the bay.','从营地出发，河流向东南弯向海湾。','to the southeast; southeast of the station','名词指东与南之间的方向或该方位地区。','The route lies between the east and south compass points.','路线位于东与南两个方位之间。'),C('southeast.s2','weather','Southeast winds pushed warm air inland, while southeast-facing windows caught the morning light.','东南风把暖空气吹向内陆，朝东南的窗户则接住晨光。','southeast wind; southeast-facing','形容词可表示来自、朝向或位于东南方。','The compound marks an orientation on the compass.','这个复合词标出罗盘上的方位。')],M('The map labels the route southeast even though it runs due west from the campsite.','The map labels the route southeast because it runs between south and east.','正西方向与东南方向不同。','distinction'),[Q(1,'In which direction does the river bend?','between south and east','between north and west','straight north','Southeast lies between south and east.'),Q(2,'What does a southeast-facing window face?','the direction between south and east','due north','the western horizon','The adjective describes its compass orientation.'),Q(1,'Where is the bay relative to camp?','to the southeast','to the northwest','directly overhead','The river bends southeast toward it.'),Q(2,'Which breeze is a southeast wind?','one coming from the southeast','one blowing from the northwest','one that has no direction','Wind names normally identify where it comes from.')]);
P('southeastern','Southeastern is formed from southeast + -ern and describes something belonging to or coming from the southeast of a region.',C('southeastern.s1','geography','The southeastern counties receive more rain because moist air moves inland from the coast.','东南部各县降雨更多，因为潮湿空气从海岸向内陆移动。','the southeastern coast/counties','形容词修饰地名，标出区域的东南部分。','These counties lie in the southeast part of the larger area.','这些县位于较大区域的东南部。'),M('The southeastern counties lie in the far northwest corner of the map.','The southeastern counties lie in the lower-right corner of the map.','地图西北角与东南部相反。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Which counties get the name southeastern?','those in the southeast part of the region','those at its northwest edge','all counties along the northern border','The suffix form describes location in the southeast.'),Q(1,'What affected rainfall there?','moist air moving inland from the coast','a dry wind from the polar north','the county’s spelling','The example links the coastal air with rain.'),Q(1,'Which is a natural phrase?','the southeastern counties','the southeastly counties','the counties southeasternly','Southeastern is the adjective form.'),Q(1,'Southeastern is built from southeast and…','-ern','-ness','-ize','The ending forms an adjective relating to a direction or region.','word-formation')]);
P('southerly','Southerly is south + -erly; it describes movement toward the south or, of a wind, one coming from the south.',C('southerly.s1','weather','A southerly breeze carried the scent of salt marshes into the harbor.','一阵南风把盐沼的气息吹进了港口。','a southerly wind/breeze; move southerly','形容词常描述来自南方的风，也可指向南移动。','The wind comes from the south and carries the smell toward the harbor.','风从南方吹来，把气味带向港口。'),M('The forecast called it a southerly wind because it blew from the north toward the south.','The forecast called it a southerly wind because it came from the south.','风向命名按来向；从北吹来的应称 northerly。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Where did the breeze come from?','the south','the north','the harbor itself','A southerly wind blows from the south.'),Q(1,'What did the breeze carry?','the smell of salt marshes','a stone bridge','a train timetable','The context says it carried the marsh scent.'),Q(1,'Which phrase fits the wind?','a southerly breeze','a southernly breeze','a southness breeze','Southerly is the established directional adjective.'),Q(1,'A ship moving southerly is moving…','toward the south','from east to west','without changing position','Southerly can describe southward movement.')]);
P('southern','Southern is formed from south with the adjective ending -ern; it means belonging to or coming from the south of an area.',C('southern.s1','geography','The southern entrance stays open in winter because it is sheltered from the prevailing wind.','南侧入口冬天仍开放，因为它避开了盛行风。','the southern coast/entrance; southern part','形容词修饰地点，表示位于或来自某一区域的南部。','The entrance is on the south side of the building.','入口位于建筑南侧。'),M('The southern entrance is on the north side of the building, opposite the map’s compass label.','The southern entrance is on the south side of the building.','建筑北侧不可能同时是其南侧入口。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Which entrance stays open in winter?','the one on the south side','the one on the north side','the entrance under the building','Southern identifies the south side.'),Q(1,'Why can it stay open?','it is sheltered from the prevailing wind','it faces the coldest wind directly','it leads to the northern entrance','The example gives shelter as the reason.'),Q(1,'What does southern modify in “southern entrance”?','the entrance’s location','the entrance’s opening time','the wind’s speed','It is a location adjective.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses the adjective naturally?','the southern coast','the southness coast','the southerning coast','Southern is the standard adjective form.')]);
P('southerner','Southerner is formed from southern + -er, naming a person from a southern region.',C('southerner.s1','identity','As a Southerner, Lena recognized the regional expressions her grandparents used in Georgia.','作为南方人，莉娜听得懂祖父母在佐治亚州使用的地区表达。','a native Southerner; a Southerner from Georgia','名词指来自某个南部地区的人。','Lena’s regional background explains her familiarity with the expressions.','莉娜的南方成长背景解释了她为何熟悉这些表达。'),M('Lena was called a Southerner because she had spent her whole life in the country’s northernmost region.','Lena was called a Southerner because she grew up in Georgia in the southern region.','只在北部生活与“南方人”的地域身份不符。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why did Lena recognize the expressions?','she came from a southern region','she had never heard them before','she had moved from the Arctic','Her southern background is stated as the reason.'),Q(1,'A Southerner is…','a person from a southern region','a person who sells souvenirs','a wind from the south','The noun names a person, not a direction or object.'),Q(1,'How is southerner formed?','southern plus -er for a person','south plus -ness for a quality','southerly plus -ize for an action','The suffix -er here names a person associated with the region.','word-formation'),Q(1,'Which spelling is used for the regional identity here?','Southerner','Southeasterner','Southness','The example capitalizes the demonym as a regional identity.')]);
P('southernmost','Southernmost combines southern + -most, meaning situated farther south than any other part of the place being described.',C('southernmost.s1','geography','Cape Meridian is the island’s southernmost point, beyond which the cliffs drop into open sea.','梅里迪安角是岛上最南端的地点，再往外便是直落入外海的悬崖。','the southernmost point/tip','最高级方位形容词指出一个范围内最靠南的位置。','No other point on the island lies farther south.','岛上没有其他地点比此处更靠南。'),M('Cape Meridian is the southernmost point even though another cape lies farther south on the same island.','Cape Meridian is the southernmost point because no place on the island lies farther south.','若岛上另有更南地点，梅里迪安角就不是最南端。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why is Cape Meridian called southernmost?','no other island point lies farther south','it is the island’s northern entrance','it is the largest cape by area','The suffix -most marks the extreme southern position.'),Q(1,'What lies beyond the cape?','cliffs dropping into open sea','a northern county','a sheltered harbor entrance','The context locates the cape at the sea cliffs.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','the southernmost point on the island','the most southernmost point','the southerner point','Southernmost already expresses the extreme position.'),Q(1,'What does -most contribute here?','the farthest or most extreme position','a person from the region','movement toward the south','It marks the southern extreme of a defined area.','word-formation')]);
P('southward','Southward combines south + -ward, meaning toward the south.',C('southward.s1','travel','The migrating cranes flew southward after the first hard frost.','第一次严寒过后，迁徙的鹤群向南飞去。','travel/head/fly southward','副词指出移动的朝向，即南方。','The flock’s route points toward the south.','鸟群的路线朝向南方。'),M('The cranes flew southward toward the Arctic Circle, far north of their starting point.','The cranes flew southward toward warmer grounds below their starting point.','朝北极圈飞行是向北而非向南。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Which way did the cranes fly?','toward the south','toward the north','toward the east only','Southward means in a southern direction.'),Q(1,'What prompted their migration?','the first hard frost','the end of a summer concert','the opening of a spa','The frost is the stated timing cue.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses southward as intended?','The boat drifted southward with the current.','The southward was painted blue.','She southwarded the letter.','Southward can modify a verb to show direction.'),Q(1,'What does -ward mean in southward?','in the direction of','the person who comes from','without the quality of','The suffix marks movement or orientation toward a direction.','word-formation')]);
P('southwest','Southwest combines south and west for the compass direction between them, and for that region or orientation.',[C('southwest.s1','navigation','The old road bends southwest just beyond the grain elevator.','旧路经过粮仓后向西南弯去。','to the southwest; southwest of town','名词指西与南之间的方位或地区。','The bend points between west and south.','弯道朝向西与南之间。'),C('southwest.s2','weather','Southwest-facing roofs receive strong afternoon sun, and southwest winds often bring dry air.','朝西南的屋顶会晒到强烈的午后阳光，西南风也常带来干燥空气。','southwest-facing; southwest wind','形容词表示位于、朝向或来自西南。','The compound specifies the roof and wind orientation.','复合词标明屋顶和风向的方位。')],M('The road bends southwest toward the northeast corner of the map.','The road bends southwest toward the lower-left corner of the map.','西南与东北是相反的方位。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Which way does the old road bend?','between south and west','between north and east','straight north','Southwest is the direction between south and west.'),Q(2,'What kind of roof gets afternoon sun?','one facing southwest','one facing due north','one with no surface','The adjective identifies its orientation.'),Q(1,'Where is the road relative to town?','southwest of it','northeast of it','directly above it','The example states the road bends southwest.'),Q(2,'A southwest wind comes from…','the southwest','the northeast','the east only','Winds are named for their direction of origin.')]);
P('southwestern','Southwestern is formed from southwest + -ern and means belonging to or situated in the southwest.',C('southwestern.s1','geography','The southwestern district includes the dry plateau and three towns near the border.','西南区包括干燥高原以及边境附近的三个城镇。','the southwestern district/border','形容词修饰地区名，表示处于一个区域的西南部。','The district occupies the southwest part of the larger map.','该区位于更大地图的西南部。'),M('The southwestern district lies in the northeast corner of the map.','The southwestern district lies in the lower-left corner of the map.','东北角和西南部彼此相反。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Which area is the southwestern district?','the one in the southwest part of the region','the one in the northeast corner','the central plateau only','Southwestern names the region’s southwest part.'),Q(1,'What does the district include?','a dry plateau and three border towns','the northern sea and one island','only the central station','Those features are listed in the context.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is idiomatic?','the southwestern border','the southwestly border','the border southwesternly district','Southwestern is an adjective before border.'),Q(1,'Southwestern differs from southeastern because it includes…','west rather than east','north rather than south','no compass direction','The compound’s first directional element changes east to west.')]);
P('souvenir','Souvenir was borrowed from French souvenir, “to remember,” from se souvenir, “remember”; English uses it for an object that recalls a visit or event.',[C('souvenir.s1','travel','Mina bought a small ceramic tile as a souvenir of her visit to the old harbor.','米娜买了一块小陶砖，作为游览旧港的纪念品。','buy/keep a souvenir of a trip','名词指为了记住某次旅行或特殊时刻而购买、保存的物品。','The tile reminds Mina of her harbor visit.','这块陶砖会让米娜想起那次港口之行。'),C('souvenir.s2','memory','The faded ticket became a souvenir of the night the band played its final show.','那张褪色的票成了乐队最后一场演出的纪念物。','a souvenir of an event','名词也可泛指能使人想起过去的事物。','The ticket serves as a reminder rather than a purchased keepsake.','票根起到回忆提示物的作用，并非专门购买的纪念品。')],M('Mina called the tile a souvenir of her trip, although it had no connection to the harbor and reminded her of nothing.','Mina kept the tile because it reminded her of her visit to the harbor.','纪念品或纪念物应当能使人想起相关的经历。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did Mina buy the tile?','to remember her visit to the harbor','to repair the harbor wall','to identify the band’s singer','A souvenir is kept as a reminder of a visit or event.'),Q(2,'What did the old ticket represent?','a reminder of the band’s final show','a map of the harbor','a ticket to a future performance','The second sense is anything that recalls the past.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a souvenir of our journey','a souvenir for remembering of journey','a souvenir at our journey','“Souvenir of” links the object to the remembered event.','collocation'),Q(1,'What is the word’s French source verb about?','remembering','digging','sowing','Souvenir comes from French souvenir, “to remember.”','word-formation')]);
P('sovereign','Sovereign came through Old French soverain from medieval Latin superanus, “above”; it names a supreme ruler and describes a country with independent governing power.',[C('sovereign.s1','government','The sovereign opened Parliament after the election, following the country’s constitutional custom.','选举后，君主按照该国宪政惯例为议会开幕。','the reigning sovereign; a sovereign ruler','名词指国王、女王或其他最高统治者。','The person formally performs a head-of-state role.','此人正式履行国家元首职能。'),C('sovereign.s2','politics','The island is a sovereign state that controls its own laws, borders, and foreign policy.','该岛是一个拥有主权的国家，自行决定法律、边境和外交政策。','a sovereign state/nation; sovereign power','形容词指能自主治理、不受外部控制。','The state makes its own governing decisions.','该国自行作出治理决定。'),C('sovereign.s3','formal','The court treated the constitution as the sovereign authority in the dispute.','在这场争议中，法院把宪法视为最高权威。','sovereign authority/power','形容词也可在正式语境中表示最高、至高无上。','No higher authority is invoked in this account.','这里没有援引更高的权威。')],M('The island was sovereign because a foreign government made all its laws and controlled its borders.','The island was sovereign because it made its own laws and controlled its borders.','受外国政府完全控制与拥有主权相矛盾。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Who opened Parliament?','the country’s supreme ruler','the elected archivist','the island’s harbor pilot','A sovereign can be a king, queen, or other supreme ruler.'),Q(2,'Why is the island a sovereign state?','it governs its own laws and foreign policy','another country controls every decision','it lies southwest of the mainland','Political sovereignty means independent governing power.'),Q(3,'What did sovereign mean of the constitution?','the highest authority in the dispute','a souvenir from a royal visit','a southern weather pattern','The formal adjective can mean supreme or highest.'),Q(2,'Which phrase uses the political adjective?','a sovereign nation','a sovereign ruler opened Parliament','the sovereign signed the law','The first phrase describes an independent state.')]);
P('sovereignty','Sovereignty is formed from sovereign + -ty; it names a country’s power to govern itself or, more broadly, supreme authority.',[C('sovereignty.s1','politics','The treaty recognized the small republic’s sovereignty and left its voters free to choose their government.','条约承认这个小共和国的主权，并让选民自由选择政府。','national sovereignty; defend/recognize sovereignty','名词指国家管理自身事务的权力。','The republic retains control over its political choices.','共和国保有自行作出政治选择的权力。'),C('sovereignty.s2','authority','The debate concerned who had sovereignty over the disputed stretch of river.','争论焦点是谁对有争议的那段河流拥有最高管辖权。','sovereignty over a territory','名词也指对某一领域或地区的最高统治权。','The parties contest who has final authority there.','双方争议谁在那里拥有最终权力。')],M('The treaty protected the republic’s sovereignty by allowing a foreign power to choose its government and laws.','The treaty protected the republic’s sovereignty by leaving those decisions to its own voters.','由外国替其决定政府和法律会削弱而不是保护自主权。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the treaty recognize?','the republic’s right to govern itself','the foreign power’s control of its voters','the river’s water level','Sovereignty is a state’s authority over its own affairs.'),Q(2,'What was disputed about the river?','who held final authority over that territory','whether the republic had a souvenir','how far the river flowed south','Sovereignty over a territory means supreme governing authority.'),Q(1,'How is sovereignty formed?','sovereign plus -ty','south plus -ward','source plus -less','The suffix forms the noun naming the condition or power.' ,'word-formation'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','recognize a country’s sovereignty','sovereignty from the river toward','a sovereignty of sovereignly','Recognize commonly takes sovereignty as its object.','collocation')]);
P('sow','Sow is Old English sawan, “to scatter seed”; the noun for an adult female pig is a separate old Germanic word, so pronunciation and history differ by sense.',[C('sow.s1','farming','The farmer sowed clover seed in the bare strip beside the orchard.','农夫在果园旁裸露的地带播下了三叶草种子。','sow seeds; sow a field with grain','动词指把种子撒进土中使植物生长。','The seed is placed in the ground for later growth.','种子被播进土里以便之后生长。'),C('sow.s2','figurative','The rumor sowed distrust between the neighbors before either family checked the facts.','两家人还没核实事实，谣言就在邻里之间埋下了不信任。','sow fear/doubt/distrust','动词比喻引发并散布一种情绪或想法。','The rumor causes suspicion to spread.','谣言使猜疑蔓延。'),C('sow.s3','farming','The sow and her piglets were moved into a clean pen before the storm.','暴风雨来临前，母猪和小猪被赶进了干净的栏圈。','a sow with piglets; breeding sow','名词指成年雌猪。','The animal is the mother of the piglets.','这种动物是小猪的母亲。')],M('The farmer sowed clover by keeping every seed sealed in a jar instead of putting any in the soil.','The farmer sowed clover by scattering its seeds into the prepared soil.','播种要把种子放进土壤，而不是全封存起来。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the farmer do with the clover seed?','put it into the soil','kept every seed in a jar','fed it to the sow','The verb sense means plant or scatter seed.'),Q(2,'What did the rumor do?','spread distrust between neighbors','restore trust immediately','grow clover in the orchard','Figuratively, sow can cause an idea or feeling to spread.'),Q(3,'Which animal was moved with piglets?','an adult female pig','a male boar','a sparrow','The noun sow means an adult female pig.'),Q(3,'Which pronunciation pattern distinction is relevant?','the seed-planting verb and female-pig noun are different words with different pronunciations','both senses always rhyme with “now”','the noun is formed from the verb by adding -ed','They are homographs with separate histories and pronunciations.','distinction')]);
P('soy','Soy entered English through Dutch soja and ultimately from Japanese shōyu, “soy sauce”; in English it can name soybeans or food made from them, and sometimes soy sauce in compounds.',C('soy.s1','food','The café offers soy in its noodle broth, and the menu identifies whether the dish contains soy sauce or beans.','这家咖啡馆在面汤中使用大豆制品，菜单还注明菜里含的是酱油还是豆类。','soy milk; soy sauce; contain soy','名词泛指大豆或以大豆制成的食品；具体制品由搭配词说明。','The menu distinguishes beans and soy sauce as forms of soy.','菜单区分大豆与酱油这两种大豆制品。'),M('The label says “contains soy,” but the recipe contains no soybeans, soy sauce, or soy-derived ingredient.','The label says “contains soy” because the broth includes soy sauce.','含有酱油就是含有大豆制品，不能同时说完全不含 soy。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does the menu’s soy label refer to?','a soybean product such as soy sauce','a wheat-only ingredient','a sparrow’s seed','Soy is the soybean or a product made from it.'),Q(1,'Which item is a soy product?','soy milk','a ceramic souvenir','a spanner','Soy milk is made from soybeans.'),Q(1,'What is the Japanese source form noted here?','shōyu, “soy sauce”','sūþ, “south”','spatium, “space”','The English word came through Dutch from Japanese shōyu.' ,'word-formation'),Q(1,'Why should a menu specify soy sauce or beans?','soy names the broader soybean product category','soy only ever means one exact noodle shape','soy is a verb meaning plant seeds','Context clarifies which soy product is present.')]);
P('soybean','Soybean combines soy + bean and names the edible seed of the Asian plant used for foods and for oil or flour.',[C('soybean.s1','agriculture','The cooperative stored each soybean crop separately until the oil mill had room to process it.','合作社把每季大豆分开储存，直到榨油厂有空处理。','soybean crop/meal/oil; grow soybeans','名词指豆科植物的可食种子，可用于制油、面粉和多种食品。','The harvested seeds are held for later processing.','收获的种子留待之后加工。')],M('The cooperative called the crop soybeans, although it had harvested only pine cones from conifer trees.','The cooperative called the crop soybeans because it had harvested the plant’s edible seeds.','松果不是大豆植物的可食种子。','word-choice'),[Q(1,'What did the cooperative store?','the plant’s edible seeds','pine cones from conifers','a set of spanners','A soybean is the edible seed of the soy plant.'),Q(1,'Why were the seeds stored separately?','the oil mill would process them later','they were already finished furniture','they had to be used as a compass','The context says processing had to wait for mill capacity.'),Q(1,'Which product comes from soybeans?','soybean oil','a southern wind','a space shuttle','Soybeans are used to produce oil.'),Q(1,'How is soybean formed?','soy plus bean','south plus bean','soy plus -ward','The compound names a bean/seed associated with soy.','word-formation')]);
P('spa','Spa takes its name from Spa, a Belgian town famed for mineral springs; English now uses it for a mineral-water resort or a center offering beauty and relaxation treatments.',[C('spa.s1','travel','The visitors soaked in the mineral pool at the old spa after a week of hiking.','徒步一周后，游客在老温泉疗养地的矿泉池里浸泡放松。','a health spa; visit a spa','名词指有矿泉水、供休养或疗养的地方。','The spring water is part of the visitors’ rest and recovery.','泉水是游客休息和疗养的一部分。'),C('spa.s2','wellness','She booked a facial and a massage at the hotel spa before the conference.','会议前，她在酒店水疗中心预约了面部护理和按摩。','a day/hotel spa; spa treatment','名词也指提供美容或放松护理的中心。','The appointments are treatments rather than mineral bathing.','预约的是护理服务，而非矿泉浴。')],M('The hotel’s spa provided facial treatments and massages, but the booking describes it as a railway repair shop.','The hotel’s spa provided facial treatments and massages in its treatment rooms.','提供美容护理的中心不是铁路维修车间。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the old spa offer?','a mineral pool for rest and recovery','a railway platform','a place to sow clover','A spa historically refers to a place with mineral water.'),Q(2,'What did she book at the hotel spa?','a facial and a massage','a flight to Spain','a spanner repair','A modern spa offers beauty or relaxation treatments.'),Q(1,'Where does the name spa come from?','a Belgian town known for mineral springs','a word for a southern wind','the name of a space shuttle','The common noun developed from the place name Spa.' ,'word-formation'),Q(2,'Which phrase fits the modern treatment-center sense?','book a spa treatment','source a spa from a supplier','sow a spa in the field','Treatment is a natural collocation for this sense.','collocation')]);
P('space','Space came through Old French espace from Latin spatium, “room, distance, or interval”; it names usable room, outer space, a gap or period, and can also mean arrange items with gaps.',[C('space.s1','interior','There is enough space beside the door for a narrow shoe rack.','门旁有足够空间放一个窄鞋架。','make/leave/find space for','名词指可供使用的空处或余地。','The empty area can hold the rack.','这块空地可以放下鞋架。'),C('space.s2','astronomy','The probe sent its first images from space beyond the Moon’s orbit.','探测器从月球轨道以外的太空发回了首批图像。','outer/deep space; travel in space','名词指地球大气层之外、星体所在的外层空间。','The probe is far beyond Earth’s atmosphere.','探测器远在地球大气层之外。'),C('space.s3','time','Leave a week of space between the two vaccination appointments.','两次疫苗接种预约之间要留出一周间隔。','a space of time; leave space between','名词可表示事物之间的距离、间隔或一段时间。','A week separates the appointments.','两次预约相隔一周。'),C('space.s4','layout','Please space the chairs evenly so wheelchair users can pass between the rows.','请把椅子均匀隔开，让轮椅使用者能从各排之间通过。','space objects evenly/apart','动词表示把物品按间隔排列。','The chairs are arranged with regular gaps.','椅子按规律留出间距。')],M('The chairs were spaced evenly by placing every chair directly against the next one with no gap.','The chairs were spaced evenly by leaving a clear, equal gap between each pair.','彼此紧贴没有间隔，不能算均匀留出空间。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Where will the shoe rack fit?','in the empty area beside the door','in the probe’s orbit','between two appointments next week','Sense 1 is usable empty room.'),Q(2,'Where did the probe send images from?','outer space beyond the Moon','the shoe rack by the door','a week-long interval','Sense 2 means the region beyond Earth.'),Q(3,'How long should separate the appointments?','one week','one hour of outer space','no time at all','Space can mean an interval of time.'),Q(4,'What should the staff do to the chairs?','arrange them with even gaps','pack them tightly together','send them beyond the Moon','The verb sense means distribute objects with gaps.')]);

})();

(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:`${w}.q${i+1}`,senseId:`${w}.s${q.s}`,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('space out','Space out combines space with out and means arrange things with gaps or periods between them, or spread them apart over an area or time.',[C('space out.s1','scheduling','The clinic spaced out the appointments by fifteen minutes to keep the waiting room from filling.','诊所把预约时间间隔十五分钟，避免候诊室挤满。','space out appointments/visits','及物短语动词，表示在事件之间留出时间间隔。','Each booking follows the previous one after a fixed interval.','每次预约与前一次之间都有固定间隔。'),C('space out.s2','layout','The seedlings were spaced out across the tray so their leaves would not overlap.','幼苗在托盘里分开摆放，以免叶片互相遮挡。','be spaced out across/along','被动结构表示物体在一片区域内分散开。','The seedlings occupy separate positions over the tray.','幼苗在托盘上各占一个位置。')],M('The clinic spaced out its appointments by booking every patient for the exact same minute.','The clinic spaced out its appointments by leaving fifteen minutes between bookings.','把所有人约在同一分钟并没有形成时间间隔。','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did the clinic space out appointments?','by leaving fifteen minutes between them','by booking all patients for one minute','by placing seedlings on a tray','The first sense means put time between events.'),Q(2,'Why were the seedlings spaced out?','to keep their leaves from overlapping','to make them arrive at the clinic','to shorten the tray','This is the distribution-over-an-area sense.'),Q(1,'Which construction takes the objects being separated?','space out the appointments','space out from the appointments to','space the appointments outly','The transitive phrasal verb takes the scheduled events as its object.' ,'grammar'),Q(2,'“The seedlings were spaced out across the tray” describes…','their positions spread over an area','a period between two meetings','someone daydreaming','The second source sense means distribute rather than keep close together.')]);
P('space shuttle','Space shuttle is a compound of space + shuttle, named for a winged spacecraft designed to launch into orbit, return to Earth, and fly again.',C('space shuttle.s1','aerospace','The space shuttle carried the repaired telescope into orbit and later glided back to a runway.','航天飞机把修好的望远镜送入轨道，之后滑翔返回跑道。','launch/land a space shuttle; shuttle to orbit','名词指可由火箭发射、带翼返回并重复飞行的航天器。','The vehicle both travels to orbit and returns by gliding.','这种飞行器既能进入轨道，也能滑翔返回。'),M('The crew flew the space shuttle beyond Earth, but it was designed only for a one-way trip and could never return.','The crew flew the space shuttle to orbit, where the vehicle could later return to Earth and fly again.','可重复返回的设计是这里 space shuttle 的关键特征。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What did the shuttle carry?','a repaired telescope into orbit','a row of chairs across a room','a mineral pool to the Moon','It carried the telescope to orbit.'),Q(1,'How did the vehicle return?','it glided back to a runway','it sank beneath the sea','it stayed permanently in orbit','A space shuttle is winged and designed to return.'),Q(1,'What does shuttle suggest in this compound?','a vehicle making a trip and return between places','a one-way object with no return','a tool for tightening bolts','The term names reusable travel to orbit and back.'),Q(1,'Which feature distinguishes the described shuttle?','it can return and fly again','it is a static satellite only','it is made from spaghetti','The vehicle was designed for repeat flights.')]);
P('spacecraft','Spacecraft combines space + craft; it is a vehicle for travel beyond Earth, including crewed ships and unmanned scientific machines.',[C('spacecraft.s1','aerospace','The crewed spacecraft carried four researchers from the station back to Earth.','载人航天器把四名研究人员从空间站送回地球。','crewed spacecraft; launch a spacecraft','名词指用于外层空间旅行的载具。','The vehicle transports people between orbital locations and Earth.','飞行器在轨道地点与地球之间运送人员。'),C('spacecraft.s2','science','An unmanned spacecraft photographed the icy moon and transmitted measurements to the research team.','一台无人航天器拍摄了冰卫星，并把测量数据传回研究团队。','unmanned spacecraft; spacecraft probe','名词也可统称无人探测设备或航天探测器。','The machine studies a planet without carrying a crew.','这台机器在不载人的情况下研究行星。')],M('The unmanned spacecraft carried a crew of twelve astronauts to the station.','The spacecraft carried no crew and sent its measurements back by radio.','明确无人意味着没有乘员。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Who traveled in the first spacecraft?','four researchers','no one; it was a probe','the harbor visitors','The first sense describes a crewed vehicle.'),Q(2,'What did the unmanned spacecraft do?','photographed the moon and sent measurements','carried four people home','opened Parliament','Sense 2 includes scientific machines sent into space.'),Q(1,'Which is a spacecraft?','a vehicle designed to travel beyond Earth','a flat-bladed garden spade','a room with empty floor area','That matches the general vehicle sense.'),Q(2,'What does “unmanned” tell us?','the machine carries no human crew','it cannot send any data','it is powered by a shuttlecock','The second example is an uncrewed probe.')]);
P('spaceman','Spaceman combines space + man and is an informal term for a person who travels in space, usually called an astronaut today.',C('spaceman.s1','aerospace','The children asked the spaceman how he slept while floating inside the orbital capsule.','孩子们问那位宇航员在轨道舱里漂浮时如何睡觉。','a spaceman in orbit; spaceman suit','名词是宇航员的通俗、较旧称呼。','He has traveled beyond Earth and answers questions about life in orbit.','他曾到地球之外旅行，并回答有关轨道生活的问题。'),M('The museum guide called the spaceman an astronaut who had never left Earth or entered a spacecraft.','The museum guide introduced the spaceman as an astronaut who had worked in orbit.','从未进入太空的人不符合这里的 spaceman 身份。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the children ask about?','sleeping while floating in orbit','growing soybeans on Earth','repairing a spanner','The person has firsthand space-travel experience.'),Q(1,'A spaceman is another term for…','an astronaut','a sovereign ruler','a person from the southern region','It names a person who travels in space.'),Q(1,'Which modern term is more usual?','astronaut','sourness','spearhead','Spaceman is an informal older label; astronaut is standard today.' ,'register'),Q(1,'Why is “spaceman” potentially dated in formal writing?','it is an informal older label for an astronaut','it names a particular spacecraft','it means a person who spaces chairs','The term is understood but less standard than astronaut.')]);
P('spaceship','Spaceship combines space + ship; it is an everyday term for a craft that travels beyond Earth’s atmosphere.',[C('spaceship.s1','science fiction','In the novel, the spaceship crossed the nebula after its crew repaired the navigation array.','小说里，船员修好导航阵列后，宇宙飞船穿过了星云。','board/fly a spaceship; spaceship crew','名词指在地球大气层之外航行的飞行器。','The craft carries a crew through outer space.','飞行器载着船员在外层空间航行。'),C('spaceship.s2','general','The museum exhibit uses “spaceship” for both crewed vehicles and robotic craft in its children’s guide.','博物馆的儿童指南把载人飞行器和机器人航天器都称为“宇宙飞船”。','a spaceship in popular usage','日常说法中可泛指用于太空旅行的各种航天器。','The guide uses a broad everyday label rather than a technical class.','指南使用宽泛的日常称呼，而非严格技术类别。')],M('The crew boarded a spaceship that was built only to travel underwater and could not leave Earth’s atmosphere.','The crew boarded a spaceship designed to travel beyond Earth’s atmosphere.','只潜水且不能进入太空的船不符合 spaceship 的定义。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Where did the novel’s spaceship travel?','through a nebula in outer space','along a southern river','underwater in a harbor','A spaceship travels outside Earth’s atmosphere.'),Q(2,'How does the children’s guide use the word?','as a broad term for crewed and robotic space craft','only for a tool that turns a bolt','as a name for a mineral spring','The everyday sense is broader than a technical vehicle category.'),Q(1,'Which compound forms spaceship?','space plus ship','south plus ship','sour plus -ship','The word is a direct compound for a ship in space.','word-formation'),Q(1,'What had the crew repaired?','the navigation array','a spade blade','a soy crop','The context says they repaired the array before crossing the nebula.')]);
P('spacious','Spacious comes from Latin spatiosus, from spatium “space”; it describes a place with ample room for people or things.',C('spacious.s1','housing','The spacious studio has room for a worktable, two bookcases, and a clear path to the door.','这间宽敞的单间公寓能放下工作桌、两个书架，还留有通往门口的通道。','a spacious room/home; spacious enough for','形容词表示面积很大、容得下许多人或物品。','The listed furniture fits without blocking the walkway.','列出的家具能放下且不挡通道。'),M('The spacious studio was so cramped that one chair filled the entire room and blocked the door.','The spacious studio held the furniture with room left for an unobstructed walkway.','拥挤到堵门表示狭小，不是宽敞。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why is the studio spacious?','it fits furniture and leaves a clear walkway','one chair fills the whole room','it has no floor area','Spacious means there is plenty of usable room.'),Q(1,'Which adjective best describes a large airy hall?','spacious','southerly','sparing','Spacious describes generous room.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a spacious office with room for visitors','a spaciously office room for','a spaceful of office','Spacious is an adjective modifying office.' ,'grammar'),Q(1,'What does the Latin source spatium mean?','space or room','a female pig','a bright disc','Spacious is related to Latin spatium, “space.”','word-formation')]);
P('spade','Spade is from Old English spadu, “digging tool”; it also names the black suit symbol in playing cards, whose name is historically linked to a word for a sword.',[C('spade.s1','gardening','Use a spade to cut a clean edge around the flower bed before lifting the turf.','先用铁锹沿花坛边缘切出整齐的边，再掀起草皮。','dig with a spade; spade the soil','名词指带长柄和扁平刃、用于挖掘的工具。','The flat blade cuts into the ground.','扁平锹刃切入土中。'),C('spade.s2','cards','Mara drew the queen of spades and placed it face up beside the other cards.','玛拉抽到黑桃皇后，把它正面朝上放在其他牌旁。','the ace/queen of spades; a spade in a deck','名词也指扑克牌中黑色尖叶形的花色。','The card bears the black pointed suit symbol.','这张牌上有黑色尖叶形花色符号。')],M('He dug the flower bed with a spade by dealing a black playing card into the soil.','He dug the flower bed with a spade, the long-handled tool with a flat blade.','黑桃牌不是挖土工具。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Which tool did the gardener use?','a long-handled flat-bladed digging tool','a queen of hearts','a telescope','The first sense is a digging implement.'),Q(2,'What did Mara draw?','the queen of the black spade suit','a garden shovel','the ace of diamonds','Sense 2 is the card suit.'),Q(1,'What is the spade’s blade used for?','cutting into soil','turning a bolt','carrying a crew to orbit','The flat blade makes it useful for digging.'),Q(2,'Which phrase refers to the card suit?','the ace of spades','spade the flower bed','a spade of soil','The plural phrase names the playing-card suit.')]);
P('spaghetti','Spaghetti is Italian, the plural form of spaghetto, a diminutive of spago “string”; English uses it for long thin pasta and, figuratively, tangled thin lines.',[C('spaghetti.s1','food','Drain the spaghetti when it is tender, then toss it with the tomato sauce.','意大利面煮软后沥干，再与番茄酱拌匀。','a plate/bowl of spaghetti; cook spaghetti','名词指细长条状的意大利面。','The strands are cooked and served with sauce.','面条煮熟后与酱汁一起食用。'),C('spaghetti.s2','technology','Behind the server rack, a spaghetti of colored cables made it hard to trace each connection.','服务器机柜后面，缠成一团的彩色线缆让人很难追踪每个连接。','spaghetti of wires/cables/code','比喻用法指细长东西纠缠成团。','The cables cross and twist rather than following clear paths.','线缆交叉缠绕，没有清晰的走线。')],M('The technician called the neatly separated cables a spaghetti because each wire ran straight in its own channel.','The technician called the tangled mass behind the rack a spaghetti of cables.','整齐分开的线缆没有缠结，不能形象地称为 spaghetti。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did they do with the spaghetti after cooking?','drained it and added tomato sauce','wound it around the server rack','used it to turn a bolt','Sense 1 is the long thin pasta.'),Q(2,'Why was cable tracing difficult?','the wires twisted into a tangled mass','the noodles were overcooked','the server was in outer space','The figurative sense compares a tangle of thin lines to pasta.'),Q(1,'What does the Italian source spago mean?','string','south','sow','Spaghetti derives from a diminutive of Italian spago, “string.”','word-formation'),Q(2,'Which phrase uses the figurative sense?','a spaghetti of cables behind the desk','a bowl of spaghetti for lunch','spaghetti with tomato sauce','The first phrase refers to a tangled mass of wires.')]);
P('Spain','Spain comes through Latin Hispania, the ancient Roman name for the Iberian region; the deeper pre-Roman origin of that name is uncertain.',C('Spain.s1','geography','Madrid is the capital of Spain, and the train crossed the country from Seville to Barcelona.','马德里是西班牙首都，火车从塞维利亚横穿该国前往巴塞罗那。','in Spain; the capital of Spain','专有名词指伊比利亚半岛上的国家西班牙。','Both cities named lie within the country.','所列两座城市都位于该国境内。'),M('The guide said Madrid is the capital of Spain, although Madrid is in Portugal and Spain is in Scandinavia.','The guide said Madrid is the capital of Spain on the Iberian Peninsula.','马德里位于西班牙；西班牙不在斯堪的纳维亚。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What is the capital of Spain?','Madrid','Lisbon','Seville','The source entry identifies Madrid as the capital.'),Q(1,'Where is Spain located?','on the Iberian Peninsula','in Scandinavia','in the southern Pacific','Spain is the country on the Iberian Peninsula.'),Q(1,'Which train route stays within Spain in the example?','Seville to Barcelona','Lisbon to Porto','Oslo to Bergen','Both named endpoints are Spanish cities.'),Q(1,'Which older name is related to Spain?','Latin Hispania','Old English sūþ','Italian spago','The English country name came through Latin Hispania.','word-formation')]);
P('span','Span comes from Old English spann, related to the distance a hand can cover; it names a distance or period and as a verb means stretch across or cover.',[C('span.s1','engineering','The new footbridge has a single span of forty metres between its concrete supports.','新的人行桥在两座混凝土支座之间有四十米的单跨。','bridge span; a span of distance','名词指桥梁或拱门两端之间的距离。','Forty metres is measured between the supports.','四十米是两端支座间的距离。'),C('span.s2','time','The archive covers a span of nearly six decades, from the first survey to the latest map.','这批档案跨越近六十年，从最早的调查到最新地图。','a span of years/time; over a short span','名词也指一段持续时间。','The dates mark the beginning and end of the period.','这些日期标出该时期的起止。'),C('span.s3','coverage','The new rail line spans three counties and connects their smaller towns.','这条新铁路横跨三个县，并连接各县的小城镇。','span a river/region/period','动词指横跨一定距离、时间范围或主题。','The route extends across the boundaries of three counties.','线路延伸穿过三个县的边界。')],M('The bridge spans forty metres, but its supports stand only a centimetre apart.','The bridge spans forty metres between its two supports.','此处四十米指支座之间的跨距，不能说只有一厘米。','measurement'),[Q(1,'What does the bridge’s forty-metre span measure?','the distance between its supports','the years in the archive','the number of counties','The structural noun sense is the distance from one end to the other.'),Q(2,'How long does the archive cover?','nearly six decades','forty metres','three counties','Span can name a period of time.'),Q(3,'What does the rail line do?','extends across three counties','lasts six decades','supports the footbridge','The verb means stretch across a region.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural for a bridge?','a single span between supports','a span of southern wind','span a bridge with six decades','The noun collocates with bridge and describes its structural distance.','collocation')]);
P('spangle','Spangle is related to spang, an older word for a small glittering ornament; as a noun it is a tiny shiny disc, and as a verb it can describe bright points scattered over a surface.',[C('spangle.s1','clothing','A silver spangle on each sleeve caught the light whenever the dancer turned.','舞者每次转身，袖子上的银色亮片都会反射光线。','sew on a spangle; a dress covered in spangles','名词指缝在布料上、会闪光的小圆片。','The tiny disc reflects light from the sleeve.','小圆片从袖子上反射光线。'),C('spangle.s1','imagery','At dusk, the first stars seemed to spangle the dark water beyond the pier.','黄昏时，最早出现的星星仿佛把码头外的黑色水面点缀得闪闪发亮。','spangle the sky/water with light','动词比喻把闪亮的小点散布在某个表面。','The stars appear as scattered points of light on the water.','星光像散布在水面上的亮点。')],M('The silver spangles on her sleeve were dull pieces of cloth that reflected no light.','The silver spangles on her sleeve were tiny reflective discs that flashed when she moved.','完全不反光的布片不符合亮片的闪光特征。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What caught the light on the dancer’s sleeve?','tiny silver discs','a pair of spectacles','a bridge support','A spangle is a small glittering ornament.'),Q(1,'How did the water seem spangled?','scattered stars made bright points on it','the pier covered it with soil','the stars formed a single dark line','The verb describes bright points spread over a surface.'),Q(1,'Which garment detail is a spangle?','a reflective disc sewn to cloth','a long digging blade','a length of spare time','The source noun sense is a tiny ornament.'),Q(1,'Which verb phrase is natural?','stars spangle the water','stars spangle from the water at noon','spangle the water with mud','The verb can describe a surface dotted with glints.')]);
P('Spanish','Spanish is formed from Spain + -ish and names the language as a noun or describes something belonging to Spain or its people as an adjective.',[C('Spanish.s1','language','Rosa speaks Spanish with her grandmother and switches to English at work.','罗莎和祖母说西班牙语，在工作时则改说英语。','speak/learn Spanish; Spanish speaker','名词指西班牙及美洲许多地区使用的罗曼语。','The example treats Spanish as a language one can speak.','这里把 Spanish 当作可以说的一种语言。'),C('Spanish.s2','culture','The museum displayed Spanish ceramics beside the maps of Andalusia.','博物馆把西班牙陶器陈列在安达卢西亚地图旁。','Spanish art/food/history','形容词表示属于西班牙、其人民或文化。','The ceramics are identified by their cultural origin.','陶器按其文化来源归类。')],M('Rosa speaks Spanish with her grandmother, but the sentence uses Spanish as the name of a type of ceramic bowl.','Rosa speaks Spanish with her grandmother as the language they share.','在 speaks Spanish 中，Spanish 是语言名而非器物名。','grammar'),[Q(1,'What language does Rosa use with her grandmother?','Spanish','Portuguese','Latin','Spanish is the language named in sense 1.'),Q(2,'What kind of ceramics were displayed?','those belonging to Spanish culture','those made from soybeans','those from the southeastern sea','Spanish modifies ceramics to mark cultural origin.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses Spanish as a noun?','She studies Spanish every evening.','They bought Spanish ceramics.','The Spanish museum reopened.','In the first sentence, Spanish names the language.'),Q(2,'In “Spanish ceramics,” Spanish is…','an adjective describing cultural origin','a verb meaning to speak','a noun for a card suit','The word modifies ceramics as an adjective.')]);


P('spank','Spank is recorded in English from the eighteenth century for striking the buttocks with an open hand; its earlier derivation is uncertain.',C('spank.s1','parenting','The parenting guide says that hitting a child is harmful and recommends calm, non-physical discipline instead of spanking.','育儿指南指出打孩子有害，并建议采用冷静、非暴力的管教方式，而不是打屁股。','spank a child; spanking as punishment','动词指用张开的手掌打臀部作为惩罚。','The sentence names the action while explicitly advising against it.','句子提到这种动作，同时明确反对这样做。'),M('The parent spanked the child by comforting them gently and never striking them.','The parent spanked the child by striking the child’s bottom with an open hand.','安慰而不击打并不是spank所指的动作。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What action does spank name?','strike the buttocks with an open hand','tap a shoulder to get attention','use a strap to secure cargo','The source sense is an open-handed strike to the buttocks.'),Q(1,'What does the guide recommend instead?','calm, non-physical discipline','more frequent spanking','a visit to a spa','The example explicitly favors non-physical discipline.'),Q(1,'Which phrase fits the verb?','spank a child','spank a saucepan with sauce','spank to a child','The verb takes the person being struck as its object.','grammar'),Q(1,'Is the guide endorsing the action?','no; it calls it harmful and recommends another approach','yes; it praises it as harmless','it says nothing about discipline','The sentence’s stated position is opposition.')]);
P('spanking','Spanking is formed from spank + -ing; it names the punishment or, as an adjective in informal use, describes a brisk pace or strong breeze.',[C('spanking.s1','parenting','The report counted spanking as a physical punishment and recommended non-violent alternatives.','报告把打屁股列为体罚，并建议采用非暴力替代方式。','corporal punishment by spanking','名词义指以拍打臀部实施的惩罚。','It is classified as a form of physical punishment.','它被归为一种身体惩罚。'),C('spanking.s1','sport','The cyclists maintained a spanking pace up the final hill despite the headwind.','尽管迎着逆风，骑行者仍以很快的速度骑上了最后一段坡。','a spanking pace; a spanking breeze','形容词在非正式用法中表示速度快或风力强劲。','The pace is brisk rather than slow.','这里的速度很快而不是缓慢。')],M('The cyclists climbed at a spanking pace, moving so slowly that they covered only one metre in an hour.','The cyclists climbed at a spanking pace, moving briskly up the hill.','每小时只走一米表示极慢，与spanking“迅速有劲”相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did the report classify spanking?','as physical punishment','as a kind of bicycle','as a wind direction','The noun sense names a punishment.'),Q(1,'What was the cyclists’ pace?','brisk and energetic','extremely slow','completely stationary','Spanking as an adjective can mean lively or brisk.'),Q(1,'Which expression uses the brisk adjective?','a spanking breeze','spanking as a punishment','to spank a child','The breeze phrase uses the adjective for strength or liveliness.'),Q(1,'How is spanking related to spank?','it is formed with the -ing ending','it is spank plus the opposite prefix','it comes from Spain','The form is the -ing derivative of spank.','word-formation')]);
P('spanner','Spanner is formed from span, “turn or stretch,” with -er, and names a hand tool whose opening fits a nut or bolt so it can be turned.',C('spanner.s1','repair','The mechanic chose a ring spanner that fitted the bolt head without slipping.','技工挑了一把正好套住螺栓头、不易打滑的梅花扳手。','ring/adjustable spanner; turn a nut with a spanner','名词指用开口套住螺母或螺栓并手动旋转的工具。','The fitted opening transfers force to turn the fastener.','贴合的开口把力传到紧固件上，使其转动。'),M('She loosened the bolt with a spanner by pressing the tool against the wall and never fitting it over the bolt.','She loosened the bolt with a spanner fitted over its head.','扳手必须套合螺栓或螺母才能转动它。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the mechanic use?','a tool fitted over a bolt','a playing card suit','a flat-bladed digging tool','A spanner is a hand tool for nuts and bolts.'),Q(1,'Why did the ring spanner not slip?','its opening fitted the bolt head','it was made of spaghetti','it was pointed south','The fitting helps the tool grip the fastener.'),Q(1,'Which collocation is natural?','turn a nut with a spanner','sow a spanner into a field','a spanner of time','A spanner is used to turn a nut or bolt.','collocation'),Q(1,'What does the tool’s opening fit?','a nut or bolt','a telescope lens','a seed coat','The opening is shaped to fit a fastener.')]);
P('spar','Spar as a verb is recorded for light boxing practice and for a testing but not necessarily hostile argument; its older word history is uncertain.',[C('spar.s1','boxing','The two boxers sparred for three rounds without trying to knock each other out.','两名拳击手进行了三回合对练，并没有试图击倒对方。','spar with an opponent; spar lightly','动词指拳击手进行较轻的练习性对打。','The round is practice rather than a full competitive bout.','这一回合是训练，而非正式比赛。'),C('spar.s1','discussion','The researchers sparred over the best way to label the samples, but agreed on the final protocol.','研究人员就样本标签的最佳写法展开了辩论，但最终同意了操作方案。','spar over/about an issue','动词也可指带有较量意味的争论或交锋。','They challenge each other’s ideas but reach agreement.','双方交锋观点，但最终达成一致。')],M('The boxers sparred for practice, but one competitor tried to knock the other out in a championship fight.','The boxers sparred lightly as a training exercise.','以击倒对手为目标的冠军赛不是轻量练习对打。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What did the boxers do?','practised lightly against each other','fought a championship bout to a knockout','fixed a bolt with a wrench','Spar in boxing means practise with controlled, light blows.'),Q(1,'What did the researchers argue about?','how to label the samples','where to buy a sparrow','whether the bridge was forty metres long','The second use means a testing discussion.'),Q(1,'Which preposition fits the discussion sense?','spar over the wording','spar into the wording','spar under the wording','Spar over an issue is a natural construction.','collocation'),Q(1,'Does spar always imply a serious fight?','no; it can be practice or a friendly challenge','yes; it always means a lethal fight','it means a person from Spain','Both senses allow a controlled or testing exchange.')]);
P('spare','Spare is from Old English sparian, “refrain or save”; as an adjective it means extra, as a verb it can give or withhold harm, and as a noun it names a replacement item.',[C('spare.s1','supplies','Keep a spare key in the office in case the main one is lost.','办公室里留一把备用钥匙，以防主钥匙丢失。','a spare key/part/room','形容词指额外保留、需要时可用的。','The extra key is kept for a possible loss.','这把额外钥匙留作丢失时使用。'),C('spare.s2','time','Could you spare ten minutes to help me check the figures?','你能抽出十分钟帮我核对数字吗？','spare time/money; spare someone a moment','动词表示把自己可以留着的时间、钱或物品给别人。','The speaker asks the other person to give a little of their time.','说话者请对方匀出一点时间。'),C('spare.s3','mercy','The guards spared the injured messenger and let her leave the compound.','守卫饶过了受伤的信使，让她离开院落。','spare someone’s life; spare a person punishment','动词也表示不伤害或不惩罚本可伤害的人。','They choose not to harm or punish her.','他们选择不伤害或惩罚她。'),C('spare.s4','equipment','The driver fitted the spare after a nail punctured the rear tyre.','后轮被钉子扎破后，司机装上了备用轮胎。','a spare tyre/part; carry a spare','名词指为替换损坏或丢失物品而留存的备用件。','The extra tyre replaces the punctured one.','额外轮胎用来替换被扎破的轮胎。')],M('The driver fitted the spare tyre, although the punctured wheel was already back on the car and no replacement was needed.','The driver fitted the spare tyre after removing the punctured wheel.','备用件用于替换损坏的原件，不会在无须替换时仍被装上。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why keep a spare key?','to use if the main key is lost','to give away the only key','to punish the messenger','Spare as an adjective means extra and kept in reserve.'),Q(2,'What does “spare ten minutes” ask someone to do?','give up a little of their available time','keep ten minutes in a locked box','avoid speaking for ten minutes','The verb means give time that one could otherwise keep.'),Q(3,'What did the guards do for the messenger?','they chose not to harm or punish her','they took her spare tyre','they asked her to label samples','Spare someone can mean show mercy or refrain from harm.'),Q(4,'What is a spare tyre?','an extra tyre kept for replacement','a tyre that has already been discarded','a tool for turning a bolt','The noun names an additional replacement item.')]);
P('spare time','Spare time combines spare, “available or not required,” with time; it means the periods when duties do not occupy someone.',C('spare time.s1','daily life','In her spare time, Noor restores old maps and records where each one came from.','努尔在空闲时间修复旧地图，并记录每张地图的来源。','in one’s spare time; use spare time to do','名词短语指工作、学习和必要事务之外的时间。','Map restoration is something Noor chooses to do outside her duties.','修复地图是努尔在职责之外自愿做的事。'),M('Noor restored maps in her spare time while every minute was required for her paid shift and assigned duties.','Noor restored maps in her spare time after her shift and other required duties were finished.','所有时间都被职责占用就没有空闲时间。','meaning'),[Q(1,'When does Noor restore maps?','when work and duties leave her free','during every required minute of her shift','only while she is asleep','Spare time is time not taken by necessary duties.'),Q(1,'What is Noor’s chosen activity?','restoring old maps','repairing spanners','sowing clover','The context names her free-time hobby.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is standard?','in my spare time','at my spare time','by my spare time','The usual expression is “in one’s spare time.”','collocation'),Q(1,'What does spare mean in spare time?','available beyond what is required','damaged and unusable','from the south','Here it means free or extra time.')]);
P('sparing','Sparing is formed from spare + -ing and describes careful, limited use or giving, without excess.',C('sparing.s1','resources','The editor made sparing use of italics, reserving them for titles and foreign phrases.','编辑很少使用斜体，只把它留给标题和外来短语。','sparing use of; be sparing with','形容词表示谨慎、节约地使用或给予，不多用。','Italics appear only in a few selected cases.','斜体只用于少数特定情况。'),M('The editor made sparing use of italics by italicizing every word on every page.','The editor made sparing use of italics, applying them only to a few titles.','每页每个词都用斜体是大量使用，不是节制使用。','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did the editor use italics?','only in a few selected places','on every word of every page','not at all because the text was blank','Sparing means careful and limited rather than excessive.'),Q(1,'Which phrase fits?','be sparing with praise','be sparing to praise with','a sparing of praising','“Sparing with” introduces something used in limited amounts.','collocation'),Q(1,'What does the example reserve italics for?','titles and foreign phrases','every punctuation mark','the map’s southern edge','Those are the limited uses specified.'),Q(1,'Sparing is related to which base word?','spare','Spain','space','It is formed from spare with the -ing adjective ending.','word-formation')]);
P('sparingly','Sparingly is formed from sparing + -ly and means using or applying only a small amount.',C('sparingly.s1','cooking','Add the chili oil sparingly at first; guests can pour in more if they want extra heat.','先少量加入辣椒油；客人若想更辣，可以再自行添加。','use/apply sparingly; sprinkle sparingly','副词修饰动作，表示少量地、节制地使用。','A small initial amount leaves room to add more later.','先加少量，之后还可再添。'),M('She used the chili oil sparingly by pouring the entire bottle into one serving.','She used the chili oil sparingly by adding only a few drops to each bowl.','倒入整瓶是大量使用，不是少量使用。','measurement'),[Q(1,'How much chili oil should be added at first?','only a small amount','the entire bottle','none of the soup','Sparingly means using only a little.'),Q(1,'Why can guests add more later?','the first amount is deliberately limited','the dish has no room for oil','sparingly means very quickly','The small initial portion allows adjustment.'),Q(1,'Which adverb has the same sense?','sparingly','spaciously','southward','Sparingly describes limited use.'),Q(1,'How is sparingly formed?','sparing plus -ly','south plus -ward','spark plus -er','-ly forms an adverb from sparing.','word-formation')]);
})();

(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:`${w}.q${i+1}`,senseId:`${w}.s${q.s}`,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('spark','Spark is from Old English spearca, “a small fiery particle”; the noun names a flying ember or a tiny amount, and the verb means cause something to begin.',[C('spark.s1','fire safety','A spark from the welding torch landed on the fireproof mat and went out at once.','焊枪溅出的一点火星落在防火垫上，马上熄灭了。','a spark from a fire/tool; flying sparks','名词指燃烧物或硬物碰撞时飞出的一小点火。','The particle leaves the torch and is extinguished on the mat.','火星离开焊枪后落在垫子上熄灭。'),C('spark.s2','emotion','Her first lesson with the new teacher rekindled a spark of confidence.','她跟新老师上的第一节课重新点燃了一点信心。','a spark of interest/hope/confidence','名词也指某种品质或情感的少量表现。','Only a small amount of confidence returns.','恢复的信心只有一点点。'),C('spark.s3','events','The leaked schedule sparked a debate about how the school chose its speakers.','泄露的日程引发了人们对学校如何挑选发言人的讨论。','spark a debate/interest; spark off a reaction','动词作及物用法，表示引发某事开始。','The leak causes the debate to begin.','泄露事件使讨论开始。')],M('The leaked schedule sparked a debate by preventing anyone from discussing it or reacting to it.','The leaked schedule sparked a debate by prompting people to discuss the selection process.','引发讨论意味着促使讨论开始，而不是阻止讨论。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What landed on the fireproof mat?','a tiny piece of fire','a piece of a bridge','a spare key','Spark sense 1 is a small flying ember.'),Q(2,'What returned for the student?','a small amount of confidence','a large stock of spare parts','a southern wind','A spark can be a small amount of a feeling or quality.'),Q(3,'What did the leaked schedule do?','started a debate','ended all discussion','turned into a welding torch','The verb means cause an event to begin.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses spark as a small flash of fire?','a spark from the torch','a spark of confidence','sparked a debate','Only the first describes a physical ember.')]);
P('sparkle','Sparkle is formed from spark with the expressive/iterative ending -le; it means shine with small flashes, show lively intelligence, or name the resulting flashes or liveliness.',[C('sparkle.s1','light','Frost made the grass sparkle in the early sunlight.','霜使草地在清晨阳光下闪闪发亮。','sparkle in the light; make something sparkle','动词指许多小光点闪烁。','The frost reflects many tiny flashes of sunlight.','霜反射出许多细小的阳光。'),C('sparkle.s2','personality','The young pianist’s explanations sparkled with wit, even during the technical rehearsal.','即使在技术排练中，年轻钢琴家的讲解也妙趣横生。','sparkle with wit/energy; eyes sparkle','动词也可形容人显得机敏、活泼而有活力。','Her remarks are lively and clever.','她的话机敏而生动。'),C('sparkle.s3','appearance','The glass beads gave the costume a little sparkle under the stage lights.','舞台灯光下，玻璃珠让戏服显出些许闪光。','a sparkle in someone’s eyes; add sparkle','名词指一串小闪光，也可指生动活力。','The beads create brief bright points on the costume.','珠子在戏服上产生短暂亮点。')],M('The frost made the grass sparkle in sunlight, but the surface remained completely dull and absorbed every ray.','The frost made the grass sparkle by reflecting many small points of sunlight.','sparkle表示闪亮，完全暗淡吸光与此相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the frost do to the grass?','made it flash with tiny points of light','covered it with a single dark blanket','caused it to produce a debate','Sense 1 is shining with small flashes.'),Q(2,'How did the pianist’s remarks seem?','lively and clever','quietly frozen','widely spaced','Sparkle can describe wit and energy.'),Q(3,'What did the glass beads add?','a little reflected brightness','a week of free time','a tool for turning bolts','The noun sparkle is the light they add.'),Q(2,'Which sentence uses the lively-personality sense?','Her conversation sparkled with quick jokes.','The frost sparkled on the grass.','A sparkle appeared on the glass.','The first describes lively wit, not physical light.')]);
P('sparks','Sparks is the plural of spark; it can refer to flying burning particles, brief electrical flashes, or fireworks that throw out bright light.',[C('sparks.s1','workshop','The grinder sent sparks across the workshop, so the crew cleared the paper from the bench.','砂轮机把火星溅得到处都是，因此工人清走了工作台上的纸张。','shower/flying sparks; sparks from a grinder','复数名词指火焰或硬物碰撞时飞出的燃烧微粒。','The hot particles come from the grinder.','这些高温微粒从砂轮机飞出。'),C('sparks.s2','electricity','A loose wire produced blue sparks when it touched the metal casing.','松动的电线碰到金属外壳时产生了蓝色电火花。','electrical sparks; a spark between wires','复数名词也指电流产生的突然闪光。','The flash is caused by an electrical contact.','闪光由电气接触造成。'),C('sparks.s3','celebration','The children watched the garden sparks rise above the fence during the permitted fireworks display.','在获准燃放的烟火表演中，孩子们看着花园焰火越过围栏升起。','light/see sparks; sparks from fireworks','复数形式还可指娱乐用烟火喷出的亮光。','The display produces showers of bright light.','表演喷出成片亮光。')],M('The loose wire produced electrical sparks, but the scene describes a steady blue glow with no sudden flash.','The loose wire produced brief blue flashes when it touched the metal casing.','电火花是突然闪光，不是持续不变的光晕。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why did workers clear paper from the bench?','hot particles flew from the grinder','a fireworks display began in the garden','the wire stopped touching the casing','Sparks in sense 1 can ignite nearby material.'),Q(2,'What made the blue flashes?','a loose wire touching metal','a grinder cutting paper','a row of glass beads','Electrical sparks are sudden flashes caused by electrical contact.'),Q(3,'What did the children watch?','bright light from fireworks','a river’s source','a row of spacers','The third use means fireworks or their showers of light.'),Q(1,'Which is a workshop spark?','a tiny burning particle from grinding','an electrical flash in a circuit','a firework lit for a celebration','The first sense is the flying hot particle.')]);
P('sparrow','Sparrow is from Old English spearwa, an old Germanic bird name; it refers to a small passerine bird commonly found near people.',C('sparrow.s1','wildlife','A sparrow hopped under the café table to collect crumbs left by the morning customers.','一只麻雀跳到咖啡馆桌子下面，啄食早晨顾客留下的碎屑。','house/tree sparrow; a flock of sparrows','名词指一种常见的小型雀形目鸣禽。','The bird is small and forages around people.','这只鸟体型小，在人类活动区觅食。'),M('The sparrow under the café table was a large marine mammal that fed on fish.','The sparrow under the café table was a small songbird feeding on crumbs.','麻雀是小型鸟类，不是海洋哺乳动物。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Which animal collected crumbs?','a small bird','a seal','a sow','A sparrow is a small passerine bird.'),Q(1,'Where did it look for food?','under the café table','inside a spacecraft','on a southern cliff only','The bird hopped under the table for crumbs.'),Q(1,'Which place often has sparrows?','near homes and cafés','only deep outer space','only open ocean','Sparrows commonly live near people.'),Q(1,'Which older form is connected with sparrow?','Old English spearwa','Latin spatium','French souvenir','The English bird name continues an Old English form.','word-formation')]);
P('sparse','Sparse is from Latin sparsus, “scattered,” the past participle of spargere, “scatter”; it describes something present in small numbers or amounts across a wide area.',C('sparse.s1','data','The first survey had sparse data from the mountain villages, so the team returned to collect more.','第一轮调查收集到的山村数据很少，因此团队再次前往补充资料。','sparse evidence/data/vegetation','形容词指数量少、分布稀疏或不充分。','Few observations were collected from a large area.','在广阔区域内只收集到少量观察数据。'),M('The report described the records as sparse even though it contained a complete observation from every household every day.','The report described the records as sparse because only a few villages had supplied observations.','覆盖所有家庭每天记录并不稀少。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why were more observations needed?','only a few villages had supplied data','the survey covered every household daily','the team had too much information','Sparse means present in small numbers or amounts.'),Q(1,'Which landscape is sparse?','a wide plain with only a few trees','a dense forest with trees every metre','a packed city square','Few scattered items over an area are sparse.'),Q(1,'What does Latin sparsus mean?','scattered','south','to remember','Sparse comes from a Latin word meaning scattered.' ,'word-formation'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','sparse evidence from the survey','sparsely evidence in a report','a sparse of three villages','Sparse is an adjective modifying evidence.')]);
P('sparsely','Sparsely is formed from sparse + -ly and means with few people or objects spread over an area.',C('sparsely.s1','population','The northern plain is sparsely populated, with only three villages along the highway.','北部平原人口稀少，沿公路只有三个村庄。','sparsely populated/vegetated','副词修饰分布或居住状态，表示数量少且分散。','The settlements are far apart across the plain.','村落在平原上相隔很远。'),M('The plain was sparsely populated, with a crowded town on every street corner.','The plain was sparsely populated, with just three far-apart villages.','每个街角都有拥挤城镇不符合人口稀少。','meaning'),[Q(1,'How are the villages distributed?','far apart with large empty areas between','crowded together at every corner','inside the same apartment','Sparsely means few and spread across a wide area.'),Q(1,'What does the adverb modify in “sparsely populated”?','the way the area has inhabitants','the color of the highway','the height of the mountains','It describes the low, spread-out population.'),Q(1,'Which word is the base of sparsely?','sparse','southern','sparing','Sparsely is built from sparse and -ly.','word-formation'),Q(1,'Which phrase is grammatical?','sparsely vegetated hills','sparsely vegetation hills','sparse vegetatedly hills','The adverb modifies the participle vegetated.')]);
P('spasm','Spasm comes from Greek spasmos, “a drawing or contraction,” through medical Latin; it names an involuntary muscle contraction or a brief intense episode.',[C('spasm.s1','health','The runner stopped when a sudden spasm tightened the calf muscle.','小腿肌肉突然痉挛收紧，跑步者便停了下来。','muscle/back spasm; suffer a spasm','名词指肌肉突然、不受控制地收缩。','The contraction happens involuntarily and stops the runner.','这种收缩是不由自主的，并使跑步者停下。'),C('spasm.s1','events','The power cut caused a brief spasm of confusion before the backup lights came on.','停电后短暂出现一阵混乱，随后备用灯亮了起来。','a spasm of laughter/anger/confusion','名词也可比喻一阵短暂而强烈的情绪或活动。','Confusion rises suddenly and lasts only briefly.','混乱突然出现，但持续时间很短。')],M('The runner described a spasm, but the calf muscle stayed fully relaxed and did not contract at all.','The runner described a spasm when the calf tightened suddenly without voluntary control.','肌肉完全放松没有收缩，不符合痉挛义。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What happened to the runner’s calf?','it contracted suddenly','it stayed relaxed throughout','it became a spare tire','A spasm is an involuntary muscle contraction.'),Q(1,'How long did the power-cut confusion last?','briefly','for several years','it never began','Spasm can name a short intense episode.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses the medical sense?','a calf-muscle spasm','a spasm of laughter','a spasm of confusion','The first phrase refers directly to an involuntary contraction.'),Q(1,'What does the Greek source point to?','a drawing or contraction','a scattered bird','a southeast wind','The source history is linked to contraction.','word-formation')]);
P('spasmodic','Spasmodic comes from Greek spasmodikos through medical Latin; it describes something occurring in brief irregular bursts rather than steadily.',C('spasmodic.s1','work','The generator made spasmodic noises during the inspection, with long quiet gaps between each burst.','检查期间发电机断断续续地发出声响，每阵噪声之间有很长的安静间隔。','spasmodic activity/noise; spasmodic bursts','形容词表示不规律、短暂地间歇发生。','The noise returns in isolated episodes rather than continuously.','噪声以零散间歇出现，而非持续不断。'),M('The generator’s noise was spasmodic because it continued at the same steady volume without a pause all day.','The generator’s noise was spasmodic because it came in irregular bursts with long pauses.','持续稳定不停的声响不是间歇发作。','distinction'),[Q(1,'How did the generator sound?','in irregular bursts separated by silence','at one steady volume without stopping','only as a low southern wind','Spasmodic describes irregular short periods.'),Q(1,'Which is a spasmodic pattern?','short episodes with long gaps','a constant unchanging stream','a single permanent sound','The adjective contrasts bursts with steady continuity.'),Q(1,'What does spasmodic modify in the example?','the generator’s noises','the inspector’s map','the machine’s color','It describes how the noises occur.'),Q(1,'What related noun names a sudden contraction?','spasm','spare','span','Spasmodic is related to spasm.','word-formation')]);
P('spate','Spate is recorded in English for a sudden flood or a large rush of events; its deeper etymology is uncertain.',[C('spate.s1','news','A spate of complaints arrived after the website changed its password rules.','网站更改密码规则后，接连收到大量投诉。','a spate of complaints/incidents','名词指短时间内发生的大量相似事件。','Many complaints arrive close together in time.','许多投诉在很短时间内接连出现。'),C('spate.s2','rivers','Heavy rain caused a spate in the narrow river, which rose above the footpath.','大雨使狭窄的河流暴涨，水位漫过了步道。','a spate in the river; a sudden spate of water','名词也可指河水突然上涨或大量涌水。','The river level rises rapidly after rain.','大雨后河水水位迅速上升。')],M('A spate of complaints means one complaint arrived over several years, with no other reports.','A spate of complaints means many similar complaints arrived within a short period.','spate表示短期内大量发生，不是多年间孤立的一件。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What followed the password change?','many complaints in a short period','one complaint several years later','a river drying completely','Sense 1 is a sudden large number of events.'),Q(2,'What did the rain cause in the river?','a sudden rise in water level','a long dry season','a spate of passwords','Sense 2 describes a flood or sudden surge of water.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses the complaints sense?','a spate of reports','a spate in the river','spate the water gently','“A spate of” introduces a large rush of similar items.' ,'collocation'),Q(2,'Is the deeper origin of spate certain here?','no; its deeper etymology is uncertain','yes, it is a Latin word for space','yes, it is formed from spade','The entry avoids claiming an unsupported root.','word-formation')]);
P('spatial','Spatial is formed from Latin spatium, “space,” with the adjective suffix -al; it concerns the size, position, or arrangement of things in space.',C('spatial.s1','design','The architect made a spatial model to show how sunlight would move through the courtyard.','建筑师制作了空间模型，展示阳光将如何穿过庭院移动。','spatial awareness/relationship; spatial model','形容词指与物体在空间中的位置、大小或关系有关。','The model represents positions and movement within the courtyard.','模型呈现庭院内的位置和移动关系。'),M('The architect’s spatial model showed positions and distances, but the report says the term refers only to flavor.','The architect’s spatial model showed where objects and light would be in the courtyard.','spatial描述空间位置关系，不是味道。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the architect’s model show?','positions and movement in the courtyard','how the soup would taste','how a sparrow sings','Spatial concerns relations and positions in space.'),Q(1,'Which topic is spatial?','the distance between two buildings','the sourness of milk','a person’s nationality','The first concerns size and position in space.'),Q(1,'Which noun can spatial naturally modify?','relationship','sourness as a taste only','southerner','Spatial relationship is a common phrase.' ,'collocation'),Q(1,'What does the base spatium mean?','space','to sow','a shiny disc','Spatial derives from the Latin word for space.','word-formation')]);
P('spatter','Spatter has a sound-imitative history, though its precise formation is uncertain; it means scatter small drops of liquid or the spots left by them.',[C('spatter.s1','cleaning','Mud spattered the lower panels of the van as it crossed the flooded lane.','货车驶过被水淹的车道时，泥点溅到了车身下部。','spatter mud/water across; spatter with paint','动词指液体以许多小滴飞溅或使某表面沾上小滴。','The moving vehicle throws droplets onto its panels.','行驶中的车辆把泥滴溅到车身上。'),C('spatter.s2','evidence','The lab technician photographed the small spatters on the sleeve before cleaning it.','实验室技术员清洗袖子前，先拍下了上面的小片溅斑。','blood/paint spatters; a spatter on the wall','名词指溅落在表面上的小点或飞溅现象。','The marks are the drops left after liquid splashes.','这些印记是液体飞溅后留下的水滴。')],M('The van spattered mud onto its panels by keeping every drop of mud inside the tyres.','The van spattered mud onto its panels as the tyres threw droplets outward.','泥滴始终留在轮胎内就不会飞溅到车身。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What happened as the van crossed the lane?','mud droplets hit its lower panels','the mud stayed inside the tyres','the van turned into a spade','The verb means scatter small drops onto a surface.'),Q(2,'What did the technician photograph?','small splash marks on the sleeve','the sleeve’s spare button','a flock of sparrows','Spatters are little marks left by splashed liquid.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','spatter the wall with paint','spatter paint under a source','a spatter of space','Spatter with identifies the liquid spread over a surface.' ,'collocation'),Q(2,'What is the status of the word’s deeper formation?','its precise origin is uncertain','it certainly comes from Latin for bird','it is a compound of south and water','The entry marks the exact formation as uncertain.','word-formation')]);
P('spawn','Spawn is recorded in Middle English for fish eggs and later for producing them; the verb also means cause many new things, often unwelcome, to appear.',[C('spawn.s1','biology','The salmon returned upstream to spawn in the gravel beds where the eggs could develop.','鲑鱼洄游到上游，在卵能够发育的砾石床中产卵。','spawn in a river; fish spawn','动词指鱼、蛙或贝类产卵。','The salmon produce eggs in their breeding area.','鲑鱼在繁殖地排卵。'),C('spawn.s2','social','The failed login system spawned a wave of support requests from locked-out customers.','登录系统故障引发了被锁定客户的一波求助请求。','spawn a debate/problem/wave of requests','动词比喻导致某种情况或大量事物出现。','The system failure causes many requests to arise.','系统故障导致大量求助出现。')],M('The salmon spawned by avoiding the river and laying its eggs in a dry office drawer.','The salmon spawned by releasing eggs in the gravel bed of the river.','这里的生物学义指鱼在水中产卵，不是在干燥抽屉里。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the salmon return upstream?','to produce eggs in the gravel beds','to repair a login system','to buy a souvenir','Spawn in the biological sense means produce eggs.'),Q(2,'What did the login failure cause?','many support requests','salmon eggs','a spanner to turn','Figuratively, spawn means cause many things to appear.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses the biological sense?','Frogs spawn in the pond each spring.','The app spawned a wave of complaints.','The debate spawned new ideas.','The first sentence refers to animals producing eggs.'),Q(2,'Which pattern is natural for the figurative sense?','spawn a wave of requests','spawn to a request from','spawn requests in a fish','The verb takes the resulting situation as its object.' ,'grammar')]);
P('speak','Speak is from Old English sprecan, a Germanic verb; it covers talking, using a language, addressing an audience, and showing or representing an idea.',[C('speak.s1','conversation','Could I speak with the lab manager after the safety briefing?','安全说明会后我能和实验室经理谈谈吗？','speak with/to someone; speak about a problem','动词指用语言与某人交谈。','The speaker requests a conversation with the manager.','说话者请求与经理交谈。'),C('speak.s2','language','Her grandparents speak Spanish at home, while the children answer in English.','她的祖父母在家说西班牙语，孩子们则用英语回答。','speak a language; speak Spanish fluently','动词也指会使用某种语言。','Spanish is the language the grandparents use.','西班牙语是祖父母使用的语言。'),C('speak.s3','public address','The engineer will speak at the public meeting about the new bridge design.','工程师将在公众会议上就新桥设计发言。','speak at/to an audience; speak on a topic','动词可指向一群人作正式发言。','The engineer addresses attendees at a scheduled meeting.','工程师在安排好的会议上向与会者讲话。'),C('speak.s4','evidence','The unusually low failure rate speaks for the quality of the new material.','异常低的故障率说明了新材料的质量。','facts/results speak for themselves','动词也可指事实清楚地表明某事，或代表某群体发言。','The results provide evidence of quality without further explanation.','这些结果无需多加解释就能证明质量。')],M('The engineer spoke at the meeting by remaining silent throughout the session.','The engineer spoke at the meeting by explaining the bridge design to the attendees.','全程沉默不构成发言。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Who does the speaker want to talk with?','the lab manager','the salmon','the southernmost county','Speak with someone means have a conversation.'),Q(2,'Which language do the grandparents use?','Spanish','Latin','Dutch','Here speak means use a language.'),Q(3,'Where will the engineer make a formal address?','at the public meeting','in the river gravel','inside a shoe rack','Speak at a meeting is the public-address sense.'),Q(4,'What does the low failure rate do?','provides evidence of the material’s quality','asks the manager a question','translates Spanish','Results can speak for or show a quality.')]);
P('speaker','Speaker is formed from speak + -er; it names a person who talks or gives a speech, and an electroacoustic device that produces sound.',[C('speaker.s1','public address','The keynote speaker thanked the volunteers before outlining the project’s next stage.','主旨发言人在介绍项目下一阶段前先感谢了志愿者。','guest/keynote speaker; invite a speaker','名词指正在说话或向公众作演讲的人。','The person addresses the audience from the stage.','此人在台上向听众讲话。'),C('speaker.s2','audio','One speaker on the left channel had failed, so the technician replaced it before the concert.','左声道的一个扬声器坏了，所以技术员在音乐会前把它换掉。','loudspeaker; a pair of speakers','名词也指把电信号转换成声音的设备。','The component reproduces the audio signal as sound.','这个部件把音频信号转换成声音。')],M('The technician replaced the speaker that gives the keynote address because the left audio channel had failed.','The technician replaced the speaker device on the left audio channel.','左声道故障指音响设备，不是演讲者。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Who thanked the volunteers?','the keynote speaker','the technician’s left speaker','the salmon','Sense 1 names the person giving the talk.'),Q(2,'What failed on the left channel?','an audio device that produces sound','the person giving a speech','a bridge span','Sense 2 is the sound-producing equipment.'),Q(1,'Which phrase names a person?','invite a guest speaker','replace a speaker on the left channel','turn up the loudspeaker volume','The guest speaker is a person invited to talk.'),Q(2,'How is speaker formed?','speak plus -er','space plus -ward','spank plus -ish','-er forms an agent noun or a device noun here.','word-formation')]);
P('speaking','Speaking is speak + -ing; it names the act or skill of talking and also modifies a noun to identify the language used by a group.',[C('speaking.s1','communication','Public speaking became easier for Ana after she practised short talks at the community center.','安娜在社区中心练习短讲后，公开演讲变得容易多了。','public speaking; improve one’s speaking','名词指说话这一行为或进行口头表达的能力。','Practice improves her oral communication skill.','练习提高了她的口头表达能力。'),C('speaking.s2','language','The English-speaking guide translated the safety rules for the visitors.','这位说英语的导游为游客翻译了安全规定。','English-speaking visitors/country','复合形容词表示使用某种口语语言的人或群体。','English identifies the language the guide uses.','English标出导游使用的口语语言。')],M('Public speaking improved Ana’s oral communication, although she never spoke or practised any spoken presentation.','Public speaking improved Ana’s oral communication through regular short talks.','公开演讲能力来自实际口头表达练习。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What became easier for Ana?','giving talks before a group','repairing a speaker device','sowing seeds','Speaking in sense 1 is oral expression or the skill of it.'),Q(2,'What language did the guide use?','English','Spanish only','the language of sparks','English-speaking identifies the language the guide speaks.'),Q(1,'Which phrase names the oral skill?','public speaking','an English-speaking guide','a speaking shuttle','Public speaking is the noun phrase for addressing an audience.'),Q(2,'In “English-speaking guide,” speaking is part of…','an adjective describing the language the guide uses','a noun for a speech skill only','a verb in the past tense','The compound adjective identifies a language user.')]);
P('spear','Spear is from Old English spere, an early Germanic weapon name; it is a long-shafted weapon with a sharp point and can also be used as a verb for thrusting or impaling.',[C('spear.s1','history','The museum displayed a bronze spear with a long wooden shaft and a narrow point.','博物馆展出了一支青铜矛，装有长木柄和窄尖头。','a hunting/bronze spear; carry a spear','名词指长柄前端带尖的武器。','Its pointed head is fixed to a long shaft.','尖头固定在长柄前端。'),C('spear.s2','cooking','The cook speared a cherry tomato with a small fork before adding it to the salad.','厨师用小叉子叉起一颗樱桃番茄，再把它放进沙拉。','spear food with a fork; spear through','动词表示用尖物刺入或叉住某物。','The fork’s tines pierce and hold the tomato.','叉齿刺入并固定番茄。')],M('The cook speared the tomato by holding it beside the fork without piercing or picking it up.','The cook speared the tomato by piercing it with the fork’s tines.','没有刺入或叉起就没有完成 spear 这一动作。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the museum display?','a long-shafted pointed weapon','an audio speaker','a wide bridge','The first sense is a pointed weapon on a shaft.'),Q(2,'How did the cook move the tomato?','pierced it with a fork','placed it beside the fork untouched','sowed it in the garden','To spear food is to pierce it with a pointed object.'),Q(1,'Which item is a spear?','a shaft with a sharp point','a flat blade used to dig','a silver ornament sewn to cloth','The defining features are a shaft and a point.'),Q(2,'Which verb phrase is natural?','spear a cherry tomato with a fork','spear a tomato from a bridge span','spear a soup with time','With names the pointed tool used.')]);
P('spearhead','Spearhead began as the pointed head of a spear; it became a verb meaning lead an initiative from the front.',C('spearhead.s1','projects','Dr. Okafor will spearhead the clinic’s vaccination drive across the three rural districts.','奥科福博士将牵头在三个乡村地区开展诊所的疫苗接种行动。','spearhead a campaign/project/reform','动词指带头组织或领导一项运动、行动或项目。','She takes the leading role in coordinating the campaign.','她承担协调行动的带头职责。'),M('Dr. Okafor spearheaded the campaign by refusing to organize it, assign roles, or take any leading role.','Dr. Okafor spearheaded the campaign by organizing teams and guiding the rollout.','拒绝组织或领导与带头推进行动相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What will Dr. Okafor do?','lead the vaccination drive','receive a souvenir','tighten a bolt','Spearhead means lead an initiative.'),Q(1,'Where will the drive take place?','across three rural districts','only in outer space','at the southwest footbridge','The context specifies the districts.'),Q(1,'Which collocation is natural?','spearhead a reform','spearhead at a reform','spearhead from a reform','Spearhead takes the initiative as its direct object.','grammar'),Q(1,'Why is the verb linked to a spear?','the spearhead is the leading point, extended metaphorically to leadership','it means make someone speak Spanish','it names a tool for tightening nuts','The noun’s leading tip provided the metaphor for taking the lead.')]);
P('special','Special came through Old French especial from Latin specialis, “particular”; it describes something unusual or made for a particular purpose, and can name a featured item or event.',[C('special.s1','events','The school arranged a special assembly to welcome the visiting students.','学校安排了一场特别集会，欢迎来访学生。','a special occasion/treat; something special','形容词指不普通、较重要或格外好的事物。','The assembly is different from an ordinary school day.','这场集会不同于普通上课日。'),C('special.s2','purpose','The lab built a special cabinet to keep temperature-sensitive samples stable.','实验室制作了专用柜，以稳定保存对温度敏感的样本。','special equipment/purpose; specially designed','形容词也指为某个特定用途制作或安排。','The cabinet is designed for a particular storage need.','柜子为一种特定储存需要而设计。'),C('special.s3','food','The café’s lunch special is lentil soup with bread for a lower price than usual.','咖啡馆的午餐特价是扁豆汤配面包，价格比平时低。','daily special; lunch special','名词指特定场合的节目、特色菜或优惠商品。','The dish is offered at a featured reduced price.','这道菜作为当日特色以优惠价供应。')],M('The café called its lunch special a special, although it was the standard full-price dish served every day.','The café’s lunch special was a featured meal offered at a lower price that day.','每天原价供应的普通菜不符合此处特价餐的含义。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why was the assembly special?','it was arranged to welcome visiting students','it was the routine daily lesson','it was a spare speaker','Sense 1 means unusual or for a particular occasion.'),Q(2,'What was the cabinet designed for?','storing temperature-sensitive samples','serving a low-priced soup','holding a spade','Special can mean designed for a particular purpose.'),Q(3,'What did the café offer?','a featured meal at a lower price','a cabinet for samples','a school assembly','The noun sense includes a daily or lunch special.'),Q(2,'Which phrase uses special in the purpose sense?','special equipment for a task','a special welcome assembly','today’s lunch special','The first phrase describes equipment made for a specific use.')]);
P('specialisation','Specialisation is the British spelling of specialization, formed from specialize + -ation; it means the process of focusing on a narrow field or that field itself.',C('specialisation.s1','education','Her specialisation in coastal ecology let the team interpret the marsh survey accurately.','她专攻海岸生态学，因此能准确解读沼泽调查结果。','a specialisation in; area of specialisation','名词指专注成为某一领域专家的过程，或该专长领域。','Coastal ecology is the narrow field she studies in depth.','海岸生态学是她深入研究的专业领域。'),M('Her specialisation in coastal ecology means she avoids focusing on any particular field and studies everything equally.','Her specialisation in coastal ecology means she concentrates on that particular field.','专门化意味着集中于一个范围较窄的领域。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What is her area of specialisation?','coastal ecology','space shuttle engineering','Spanish literature only','The term names the narrow field in which she has expertise.'),Q(1,'Why could she interpret the survey?','she had focused on coastal ecology','she had never studied the coast','she had built the marsh','Specialisation is focused study or expertise.'),Q(1,'Which spelling is British?','specialisation','specialization','specializeation','British English uses -isation here.','spelling'),Q(1,'What does -ation form in this word?','a noun naming a process or field','an adjective meaning without','a person who speaks','The suffix forms a noun from specialize.')]);
P('specialist','Specialist is special + -ist, a person with focused knowledge or training; it also names a doctor who treats one body area or type of illness.',[C('specialist.s1','work','The museum hired a textile specialist to assess the age and weave of the damaged banner.','博物馆聘请一位纺织品专家鉴定受损旗帜的年代和织法。','a specialist in textiles; consult a specialist','名词指在某一学科或工作领域有专门知识和训练的人。','Her expertise is concentrated on textiles.','她的专长集中在纺织品方面。'),C('specialist.s2','medicine','The family doctor referred him to a heart specialist after the irregular rhythm continued.','心律不齐持续出现后，家庭医生把他转诊给心脏专科医生。','heart/skin specialist; see a specialist','名词也指只治疗某类疾病或身体部位的医生。','The physician focuses on heart conditions.','这位医生专门处理心脏疾病。')],M('The textile specialist was hired to advise on fabric, but the sentence says she had no training or knowledge of textiles.','The textile specialist was hired because she had focused knowledge of fabrics and weaving.','没有相关知识或训练就不符合专家身份。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the museum hire her?','she had focused knowledge of textiles','she treated heart disease','she designed the space shuttle','A specialist has deep knowledge in a field.'),Q(2,'Who received the referral?','a doctor focused on heart conditions','a museum textile conservator','a southern wind','Sense 2 is a doctor specializing in one body area or illness.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a specialist in textile conservation','a textile specialist of with','specialist textilely work','“A specialist in” introduces the field of expertise.' ,'collocation'),Q(2,'What kind of specialist treats an irregular heart rhythm?','a heart specialist','a shoe specialist','a river-source specialist','The second sense is a doctor with a focused medical specialty.')]);
})();

(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:`${w}.q${i+1}`,senseId:`${w}.s${q.s}`,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('speciality','Speciality is related to special and ultimately Latin specialis, “particular”; British English uses it for an area of expertise or a distinctive dish or product.',[C('speciality.s1','work','Botanical illustration is Priya’s speciality, and the gallery asks her to lead the workshop.','植物插画是普里娅的专长，画廊请她带领工作坊。','one’s speciality; a speciality in a subject','名词指某人熟悉或擅长的领域或技能。','She is asked to teach the field in which she has expertise.','她受邀教授自己擅长的领域。'),C('speciality.s2','food','The inn’s speciality is a plum tart made with fruit from the orchard behind it.','这家旅店的招牌是用后方果园水果制作的李子挞。','house/local speciality; the speciality of the region','名词也可指某地或某店以之闻名的菜品或产品。','The tart is the item the inn is known for.','这道挞是旅店的知名特色。')],M('Botanical illustration was Priya’s speciality, although she had no knowledge or experience in the subject.','Botanical illustration was Priya’s speciality because she had years of focused practice.','专长意味着熟悉或擅长，完全没有经验与此相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the gallery ask Priya to lead the workshop?','botanical illustration was her area of expertise','it was the inn’s plum tart','she had never studied plants','Speciality sense 1 is a field or skill someone knows well.'),Q(2,'What is the inn known for?','its plum tart','Priya’s drawing class','a southern wind','Sense 2 can mean a distinctive dish or product.'),Q(1,'Which phrase names a field of expertise?','botanical illustration is her speciality','the inn serves a plum speciality','a special room is wide','The first phrase uses speciality for an expert field.'),Q(2,'Which phrase uses the food sense?','the restaurant’s local speciality','a doctor’s speciality in cardiology','a speciality in botanical drawing','The first phrase refers to a signature dish or product.')]);
P('specialization','Specialization is the American spelling of specialisation; it is specialize + -ation and names focused work or study in one field.',C('specialization.s1','education','The laboratory’s specialization in coastal chemistry helps it monitor salt levels in the estuary.','该实验室专攻海岸化学，因此能监测河口的盐度。','specialization in a field; area of specialization','名词指把工作或学习范围集中在某一领域的过程或结果。','Coastal chemistry is the lab’s narrow focus.','海岸化学是实验室专注的狭窄领域。'),M('The laboratory’s specialization in coastal chemistry means it avoids any narrow field and studies every subject equally.','The laboratory’s specialization in coastal chemistry means it focuses on that field.','专门化正是把工作或学习集中到特定领域。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does the laboratory focus on?','coastal chemistry','every subject equally','plum tart baking','Specialization names focused work in a particular field.'),Q(1,'Why can the lab monitor estuary salt?','its staff concentrate on coastal chemistry','it has no scientific focus','the estuary is a spacecraft','The specialization provides the relevant expertise.'),Q(1,'Which spelling is American English?','specialization','specialisation','specializeation','American spelling uses -ization.' ,'spelling'),Q(1,'What does the suffix -ation make here?','a noun for a process or result','a person who specializes','an adjective meaning without','Specialize plus -ation forms the noun specialization.','word-formation')]);
P('specialize','Specialize is special + -ize, a verb meaning focus one’s work on a field or, in biology, develop a feature adapted to a particular way of life.',[C('specialize.s1','career','After residency, Dr. Chen chose to specialize in pediatric heart disease.','住院医师培训后，陈医生选择专攻儿童心脏病。','specialize in medicine/science; specialize as a surgeon','动词表示专门从事或专攻某一领域。','The doctor directs most training and work to one medical field.','医生把大部分训练和工作集中到一个医学领域。'),C('specialize.s2','biology','Over many generations, the island finch evolved a beak specialized for cracking hard seeds.','经过许多代，岛上的雀类进化出适合啄开硬种子的喙。','species specialize for/in a niche','生物学义表示发展出适应某种生活方式的形态或特征。','The beak’s form suits a specific food source.','喙的形状适合一种特定食物来源。')],M('Dr. Chen specializes in pediatric cardiology, but she has never trained or worked in any medical area.','Dr. Chen specializes in pediatric cardiology after focused medical training.','专攻某领域意味着接受相关训练并以此为工作方向。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What field did Dr. Chen choose?','pediatric heart disease','island ecology','plum farming','Specialize in names focused study or work.'),Q(2,'What is the finch’s beak adapted to do?','crack hard seeds','treat children’s hearts','carry a space crew','In biology, specialize can describe an evolved feature suited to a niche.'),Q(1,'Which preposition follows specialize for a field?','specialize in cardiology','specialize at cardiology into','specialize of cardiology','The standard pattern is specialize in a subject.','collocation'),Q(2,'Which sentence uses the biological sense?','The moth evolved wings specialized for night flight.','She specializes in tax law.','The doctor chose a specialty.','The first describes an adapted biological feature.')]);
P('specialized','Specialized is the past participle of specialize, used as an adjective for something developed or designed for one particular task or field.',C('specialized.s1','equipment','The clinic bought a specialized scanner that can image tiny blood vessels in the eye.','诊所购入一台专用扫描仪，能够成像眼部细小血管。','specialized equipment/training; highly specialized','形容词表示为某个特定任务、群体或学科开发或设计。','The scanner’s functions address a narrowly defined medical task.','扫描仪的功能针对一个范围明确的医疗任务。'),M('The specialized scanner was intended for a precise eye-imaging task, but it had been designed for no particular use.','The specialized scanner was designed specifically to image tiny vessels in the eye.','针对特定用途设计与“没有任何特定用途”相矛盾。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What can the specialized scanner image?','tiny blood vessels in the eye','a country’s southern border','a fireworks display','It is designed for a particular medical task.'),Q(1,'What does specialized modify?','a scanner developed for a narrow purpose','a standard device for every unrelated task','a person from the south','The adjective marks a focused design.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','specialized training for the procedure','specializedly train of the procedure','a specialize training procedure','Specialized is the adjective before training.' ,'grammar'),Q(1,'What is specialized derived from?','specialize','speciality plus -er','species plus -ward','It is the past participle form of specialize.' ,'word-formation')]);
P('specially','Specially is special + -ly and means for one particular purpose, rather than in a general or incidental way.',C('specially.s1','purpose','The shelter prepared a room specially for residents who need step-free access.','避难所专门为需要无台阶通行的居民准备了一间房。','specially designed/created for; specially for','副词修饰准备或设计，强调事物是为特定目的而安排的。','The room is intentionally adapted to meet an access need.','房间经过有意安排以满足通行需求。'),M('The shelter prepared a room specially for step-free access, but it was not planned or adapted for that purpose at all.','The shelter prepared a room specially for step-free access by choosing an accessible entrance and layout.','“专门为某目的”表示有意安排，而非完全未经规划。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why was the room prepared specially?','to provide step-free access','to store a southern wind','to display a spade','Specially means for a particular purpose.'),Q(1,'What did the shelter do?','planned an accessible room','made no accommodation at all','closed every entrance','The example describes an intentional adaptation.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','specially designed for children','special designedly for children','designed special for children','Specially modifies the participle designed.' ,'grammar'),Q(1,'How is specially formed?','special plus -ly','special plus -ness','south plus -ly','The suffix -ly forms this adverb.')]);
P('specialty','Specialty is the American spelling related to special; it means a field of expertise or a food or product a place is particularly known for.',[C('specialty.s1','medicine','Neurology is Dr. Alvarez’s specialty, so she reviews the difficult seizure cases.','神经病学是阿尔瓦雷斯医生的专科，因此她负责审查棘手的癫痫病例。','medical specialty; a specialty in neurology','名词指某人特别擅长的工作或研究领域。','The doctor’s expertise makes her responsible for those cases.','医生的专长使她负责这些病例。'),C('specialty.s2','food','The bakery’s specialty is a rye loaf with caraway seeds, baked fresh each morning.','这家面包店的招牌是每天早晨新鲜烤制的葛缕子黑麦面包。','house specialty; local specialty','名词也指某店或某地特别出名的食品或产品。','The loaf is the bakery’s distinctive product.','这款面包是面包店的特色产品。')],M('Neurology is Dr. Alvarez’s specialty, although she has no training in the subject and treats no neurological cases.','Neurology is Dr. Alvarez’s specialty because she is trained to treat neurological conditions.','没有受训且不处理该类病例就不构成医学专长。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Which cases does Dr. Alvarez review?','difficult seizure cases','bakery orders','bridge repairs','Her medical specialty is neurology.'),Q(2,'What is the bakery known for?','a fresh rye loaf with caraway','a neurology clinic','a southernmost cape','The food sense is a product for which a place is known.'),Q(1,'Which spelling is common in American English?','specialty','speciality','specialtee','Specialty is the usual American spelling.' ,'spelling'),Q(2,'Which phrase uses specialty for a food?','the bakery’s specialty','a doctor’s specialty in neurology','a field of medical specialty','The first phrase refers to a signature product.')]);
P('species','Species is from Latin species, “kind, appearance,” related to specere, “to look”; it names a biological group or, formally, a kind of thing, and its plural is also species.',[C('species.s1','biology','The field team identified a species of orchid that had not been recorded in the valley before.','野外团队鉴定出一种此前未在山谷记录过的兰花。','a species of plant; endangered species','名词指能够繁殖并产生同类后代的一组相似动植物。','The orchid group is treated as a distinct biological kind.','这组兰花被视为独立的生物种类。'),C('species.s2','formal','The handbook lists several species of error that can occur when dates are entered manually.','手册列出了手动输入日期时可能出现的几种错误。','a species of something; species of risk','较正式用法中也可指一种或一类事物。','The handbook groups the errors into kinds.','手册把错误分成不同种类。')],M('The report described three species of orchid, but then said species must add -s in the plural and wrote “three specieses.”','The report described three species of orchid; species has the same form in singular and plural.','species 的复数形式仍是 species，不加 -es。','plural'),[Q(1,'What did the team identify?','a biological group of orchid','a type of calendar error','a southern direction','Species sense 1 names a group of similar organisms.'),Q(2,'What does “species of error” mean?','a kind of error','a single orchid specimen','the people who record dates','The formal use means kind or sort.'),Q(1,'What is the plural of species?','species','specieses','specie','The plural form is identical to the singular.' ,'plural'),Q(1,'What Latin verb is species related to?','specere, “to look”','sow, “to plant”','spatium, “space”','The Latin noun is associated with appearance and looking.','word-formation')]);
P('specific','Specific comes through Latin specificus, “of a particular kind,” related to species; it means clear and exact or relating to one particular person, thing, or purpose.',[C('specific.s1','instructions','Please give a specific example of the error rather than saying the form is “often confusing.”','请举一个具体的错误例子，不要只说这种形式“经常令人困惑”。','a specific example/detail; be specific about','形容词指明确、精确而非含糊。','The request calls for one exact example.','这个要求需要一个明确的例子。'),C('specific.s2','purpose','This adapter is specific to the older camera model and will not fit the new body.','这个转接器专用于较老的相机型号，不能装在新机身上。','specific to a model/person; a specific purpose','形容词也表示专属于某一对象或特定用途。','The adapter works only with the named camera model.','转接器只能与指定相机型号配合使用。'),C('specific.s3','details','Before booking, ask the guide for the specifics of the overnight route.','预订前，向导会说明夜间路线的具体细节。','the specifics of a plan; discuss specifics','名词复数可表示某事的具体细节。','The requested facts are exact route details.','所问内容是路线的精确细节。')],M('The instructions were specific, but they provided no exact example, number, or detail at all.','The instructions were specific because they named the exact error and gave an example.','缺少任何明确细节属于含糊，不是 specific。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the editor ask for?','an exact example of the error','a vague comment only','a list of camera models','Specific sense 1 means clear and exact.'),Q(2,'Which adapter fits the older camera?','the one designed for that model','any adapter regardless of model','a bridge support','Specific to means intended for one particular thing.'),Q(3,'What are “the specifics” of the route?','its exact details','a general opinion about travel','the camera’s physical size','The plural noun means precise details.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses specific as an adjective?','a specific date for the meeting','the specifics of the route','the two species in the valley','The first phrase describes an exact date.')]);
P('specifically','Specifically is specific + -ally; it means in clear exact terms, singles out one item, or introduces a more precise explanation.',[C('specifically.s1','instructions','The form asks specifically for the applicant’s current address, not a mailing address from last year.','表格明确要求填写申请人目前的住址，而不是去年的邮寄地址。','state/ask specifically; specifically request','副词表示明确、具体地说明要求。','The present address is requested in exact terms.','要求明确针对现住址。'),C('specifically.s2','selection','The grant is for rural clinics, specifically those without a full-time pharmacist.','这项拨款面向乡村诊所，尤其是没有全职药剂师的诊所。','specifically those/for; and specifically','副词可用于特别指出某一对象或子类。','The clause singles out one subgroup of rural clinics.','从句特别指出一类乡村诊所。'),C('specifically.s3','clarification','The shipment is delayed because, specifically, the customs form lacks the required signature.','货物延误的具体原因是海关表格缺少规定的签名。','more specifically; specifically, + explanation','副词也可引出对前一句内容的精确说明。','The sentence supplies the exact cause of the delay.','句子给出了延误的确切原因。')],M('The form asks specifically for a current address, but the applicant submits a vague statement about where people live in general.','The form asks specifically for the applicant’s current street address.','具体要求应提供明确项目，泛泛的陈述不符合要求。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What address does the form request?','the applicant’s current address','any address from last year','the clinic’s mailing address','Specifically makes the requested information exact.'),Q(2,'Which clinics receive particular attention?','those without a full-time pharmacist','all clinics in cities','clinics with many pharmacists','Sense 2 singles out one subgroup.'),Q(3,'What exact reason explains the delay?','the customs form lacks a signature','the weather may be bad','the shipment is generally important','Specifically introduces the precise cause.'),Q(2,'Which sentence singles out a subgroup?','The award supports nurses, specifically those working nights.','The form asks specifically for a date.','Specifically, the form lacks a signature.','The first specifically introduces a selected subgroup.')]);
P('specification','Specification is specify + -ation; it names a detailed statement of required design or a clear description of what is needed.',[C('specification.s1','engineering','The supplier checked every specification for the pump, including its pressure limit and inlet diameter.','供应商核对了水泵的每项规格，包括压力上限和进水口直径。','meet/follow a specification; product specifications','名词指对产品必须具备哪些特征或如何制造的详细要求。','The figures define the pump’s required design limits.','这些数据规定了水泵的设计限制。'),C('specification.s2','contracts','The contract includes a specification of the services required during the first month.','合同明确说明了第一个月所需提供的服务。','a specification of requirements; provide a specification','名词也指对所需内容作出的清楚、详细说明。','The contract lists exactly which services are expected.','合同逐项列出预期服务。')],M('The pump met its specification even though its pressure exceeded the stated limit and its inlet was the wrong size.','The pump met its specification by staying within the pressure limit and using the required inlet size.','超过限制且尺寸错误就是未达到规格。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Which details did the supplier check?','pressure limit and inlet diameter','the pump’s color only','the clinic’s opening hours','A product specification states required technical features.'),Q(2,'What did the contract specify?','the services required in the first month','the pump’s source in a river','the date of a southern storm','Sense 2 is a detailed statement of needs.'),Q(1,'Which verb commonly pairs with specification?','meet a specification','speak a specification into','a specification sparingly','Products can meet or fail to meet requirements.','collocation'),Q(1,'How is specification formed?','specify plus -ation','specific plus -less','species plus -ward','The suffix turns the verb into a requirement statement noun.','word-formation')]);
P('specificity','Specificity is specific + -ity; it names exactness or, in testing, the ability to correctly exclude cases that do not have the condition.',[C('specificity.s1','writing','The reviewer asked for greater specificity, including the date, location, and name of the responsible office.','审阅者要求更具体，补上日期、地点和负责办公室的名称。','lack/need specificity; with greater specificity','名词指表达指向明确对象、细节清楚的程度。','The added facts make the statement more exact.','补充的事实使陈述更精确。'),C('specificity.s1','medicine','The screening test’s specificity was high, so few healthy patients received false positive results.','这种筛查测试的特异度很高，因此很少有健康患者出现假阳性结果。','test specificity; sensitivity and specificity','医学统计中，specificity指识别阴性者的能力，也就是排除假阳性的能力。','A high value means healthy cases are usually classified as negative.','数值高意味着健康病例通常被判为阴性。')],M('The test had high specificity because it produced false positives in nearly every healthy patient.','The test had high specificity because it correctly returned negative results for most healthy patients.','健康者频繁出现假阳性表示特异度低而非高。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What facts would add specificity to the review?','date, location, and responsible office','a general statement that “things happened”','the color of the reviewer’s desk','Specificity means precision and identifiable detail.'),Q(1,'What happened to healthy patients in the high-specificity example?','few received false positive results','nearly all tested positive','they were all left untested','High specificity reduces false positives among people without the condition.'),Q(1,'What is the common adjective related to specificity?','specific','spatial','speciality','Specificity is the noun formed from specific.' ,'word-formation'),Q(1,'Which phrase fits?','the specificity of the report','specificityly of the report','a specificities of report','Specificity is an abstract noun for exactness.')]);
P('specifics','Specifics is the plural of specific used as a noun; it means the exact facts or details of a matter.',C('specifics.s1','planning','We agreed on the date and venue, but the specifics of the transport plan still need to be settled.','我们已确定日期和地点，但交通方案的具体细节仍需商定。','the specifics of a plan; discuss/confirm specifics','复数名词指某事的精确细节，而非总体想法。','Routes, times, and vehicles remain to be decided.','路线、时间和车辆尚待决定。'),M('They discussed the specifics of transport by refusing to consider any exact route, time, or vehicle.','They discussed the specifics of transport by agreeing on routes, times, and vehicles.','拒绝讨论具体信息与讨论 specifics 矛盾。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What has already been agreed?','the date and venue','every transport detail','the visitor’s language','The context distinguishes settled facts from unresolved details.'),Q(1,'What still needs to be settled?','transport routes, times, and vehicles','the meaning of southward','the bakery’s specialty','These are the exact details called the specifics.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','the specifics of the plan','a specifics of plan','specifically of the plan details','“The specifics of” introduces detailed facts.' ,'collocation'),Q(1,'Is specifics singular or plural here?','plural','singular with -s only for possession','a verb form','It is a plural noun referring to multiple details.' ,'plural')]);
P('specified','Specified is the past participle of specify; as an adjective it means clearly stated or officially required.',C('specified.s1','rules','Only the specified materials may be used for the repair; the manual lists copper tubing and two seals.','维修只能使用规定材料；手册列出了铜管和两个密封圈。','the specified time/amount; as specified in','形容词表示已被清楚指出或规定的内容。','The manual explicitly names which materials are allowed.','手册明确列出了允许使用的材料。'),M('The specified materials were copper tubing and two seals, although the technician used an unnamed substitute instead.','The specified materials were copper tubing and two seals, as listed in the manual.','未列出的替代材料不是规定中明确指定的材料。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Which materials were specified?','copper tubing and two seals','any substitute the technician chose','a set of spades','The manual clearly lists the required materials.'),Q(1,'What does specified mean here?','clearly stated or required','left completely undecided','spread sparsely over an area','Specified means explicitly named.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is idiomatic?','as specified in the manual','specified by the manually','the specification specifiedly','The standard expression is “as specified in.”','collocation'),Q(1,'What is specified the past form of?','specify','specialize','spectacle','Specified is the past participle of specify.','word-formation')]);
P('specify','Specify comes from Latin specificare, “to determine particularly”; it means state exact information or designate a required item, method, or condition.',[C('specify.s1','forms','Please specify the day and time of arrival on the booking form.','请在预订表上注明抵达的日期和时间。','specify a date/amount; specify that + clause','动词指清楚写出事实、数字或要求。','The form needs an exact day and time.','表格需要准确的日期和时间。'),C('specify.s2','contracts','The contract specifies stainless steel for the outdoor handrail.','合同规定室外扶手必须使用不锈钢。','specify a material/condition; be specified for','动词也指规定必须使用或完成的具体项目。','The material is a required choice, not merely an example.','这种材料是强制选项，而不只是示例。')],M('The booking form asks guests to specify an arrival time, but they leave the field blank and provide no time.','The booking form asks guests to specify an arrival time, and they enter 14:30.','空白未提供明确时间，不能算已经注明。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What information should guests specify?','their arrival day and time','their general opinion of travel','the room’s southern wall','Specify means state exact information.'),Q(2,'What material does the contract require?','stainless steel','any material the contractor prefers','wooden spades','The second sense means designate a required material.'),Q(1,'Which pattern is grammatical?','specify the date','specify to the date','specify at a date of','Specify takes the detail directly as its object.','grammar'),Q(2,'Which sentence uses specify to mean require a material?','The plan specifies copper pipe for the supply line.','Please specify your arrival hour.','She specialized in plumbing.','The first sentence designates a required construction item.')]);
P('specimen','Specimen is from Latin specimen, “a sign, proof, or sample,” related to specere, “to look”; it names a sample for study or a single representative example.',[C('specimen.s1','laboratory','The laboratory sealed a water specimen from the well before sending it for chemical analysis.','实验室把一份井水样本密封后送去做化学分析。','a blood/water specimen; collect a specimen','名词指用于检测、研究或展示的一小份样品。','The water is collected as a sample for testing.','水被采集作检测样本。'),C('specimen.s2','example','The guide described the ancient coin as a fine specimen of early local minting.','导览员把这枚古币称为早期当地铸币的典型实例。','a specimen of a type; a fine specimen','名词也可指某种人、动物或物品中的一个实例。','The coin represents the style of early local production.','这枚硬币代表早期当地制造风格。')],M('The lab called the water a specimen but poured it away before collecting or testing any sample.','The lab sealed a measured water sample and labeled it as the specimen for analysis.','没有收集样本却称其为检测标本，不符合语境。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the laboratory seal?','a water sample from the well','a finished coin','a map of Spain','A specimen is a sample collected for testing.'),Q(2,'Why was the coin called a specimen?','it represented an early local minting style','it was a water sample','it was the only bridge in the area','Sense 2 is a representative example of a kind.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','collect a specimen for analysis','specimen an analysis from','a specimen of analyzing','A specimen is collected before it is analyzed.','collocation'),Q(2,'Which word can replace specimen in “a specimen of early minting”?','example','schedule','specialist','Here specimen means a representative example.')]);
P('speck','Speck is recorded in Middle English for a tiny spot or particle; its deeper origin is uncertain.',[C('speck.s1','cleaning','A dark speck on the white tile turned out to be a fleck of dried paint.','白色瓷砖上的一个黑点原来是一小片干掉的油漆。','a speck of dust/paint; a dark speck','名词指表面上很小且不需要的斑点。','The paint mark is visible against the white tile.','油漆污点在白瓷砖上很明显。'),C('speck.s2','scale','From the ridge, the boat looked like a speck on the distant water.','从山脊上看，那艘船像远处水面上的一个小点。','a speck in the distance; not a speck of','名词也指极小的微粒或少量。','The boat appears extremely small at that distance.','距离使船看起来极小。')],M('The boat looked like a speck from the ridge, although it filled the entire horizon and hid the water.','The boat looked like a tiny speck against the broad stretch of distant water.','占满整个地平线的物体不可能看起来像极小一点。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What was the dark mark on the tile?','a tiny fleck of dried paint','a full coat of fresh paint','a card suit','A speck can be a very small unwanted mark.'),Q(2,'How large did the boat appear?','extremely small in the distance','large enough to fill the horizon','larger than the ridge','The second sense emphasizes a tiny object or amount.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses speck for a particle?','a speck of dust','a speck of the map’s direction','to speck into the water','“A speck of dust” names a very small particle.'),Q(1,'Is its deeper history asserted with certainty?','no; it is uncertain','yes, it is from Latin for species','yes, it is from a modern computer term','The entry states only the attested Middle English use.')]);
P('speckle','Speckle is related to speck, with -le forming a small-mark word; it names a tiny spot, often of a contrasting color.',C('speckle.s1','appearance','The brown eggshell has a pale blue base with a dark speckle near one end.','这枚棕色蛋壳底色浅蓝，一端附近有一个深色小斑点。','a dark/colorful speckle; speckles on a surface','名词指表面上一个颜色不同的小点。','The mark contrasts with the shell’s blue base.','斑点与蛋壳的蓝色底色形成对比。'),M('The eggshell had a dark speckle, but the mark was a broad, uniform band covering half the shell.','The eggshell had a tiny dark spot against its pale blue surface.','覆盖半个表面的宽色带不是一个小斑点。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What mark appeared on the shell?','a tiny dark spot','a broad half-shell band','a metal spanner','A speckle is a small mark of a different color.'),Q(1,'Why was the speckle visible?','it contrasted with the pale blue base','the shell had no other color','the shell was a southernmost point','The spot differs in color from the surface.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a speckle on the eggshell','a speckle of a whole shell covering half','specklely egg in','A speckle is a small surface mark.'),Q(1,'Which word is closely related?','speck','space','speaker','Speckle is built around the related word speck.','word-formation')]);
P('spectacle','Spectacle comes from Latin spectaculum, “a show or sight,” from spectare, “to look at”; it can mean an impressive public sight, an embarrassing scene, or (usually plural) eyeglasses.',[C('spectacle.s1','public event','The night launch was a spectacular spectacle, drawing families to the riverbank to watch the rocket climb.','夜间发射十分壮观，许多家庭聚集到河岸观看火箭升空。','a magnificent spectacle; make a spectacle of','名词指令人印象深刻的公开表演或景象。','The crowd gathers to watch a striking public event.','人群聚集观看引人注目的公开场面。'),C('spectacle.s2','embarrassment','He made a spectacle of himself by shouting at the referee until the match was stopped.','他一直冲裁判大喊，直到比赛暂停，闹出了笑话。','make a spectacle of oneself','名词也指引人注目而显得愚蠢或丢人的场面。','The outburst attracts attention and embarrasses him.','这次爆发引来注意，让他显得尴尬。'),C('spectacle.s3','vision','Without her spectacles, Dr. Wu could not read the small labels on the specimen jars.','没有眼镜，吴医生就看不清标本瓶上的小标签。','wear/put on spectacles; a pair of spectacles','名词复数 spectacles 指戴在眼前帮助看清的镜片和镜框。','The lenses correct her vision so she can read.','镜片矫正视力，让她能够阅读。')],M('He made a spectacle of himself by behaving quietly and drawing no one’s attention during the ceremony.','He made a spectacle of himself by shouting until the ceremony had to stop.','无人注意的安静举止不是引人注目的尴尬场面。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did families gather at the riverbank?','to watch an impressive rocket launch','to laugh at an embarrassing argument','to buy a pair of eyeglasses','Sense 1 is an impressive public sight.'),Q(2,'What did the man do?','created an embarrassing scene','gave a quiet speech unnoticed','looked at a specimen through lenses','Make a spectacle of oneself means behave in a conspicuously foolish way.'),Q(3,'What could Dr. Wu not read without spectacles?','small labels on specimen jars','the river’s source','a sparrow’s song','Sense 3 means eyeglasses.'),Q(3,'Which phrase uses the vision sense?','put on a pair of spectacles','a grand spectacle over the river','make a spectacle of himself','Only the first refers to eyewear.')]);
P('spectacles','Spectacles is the plural form of spectacle used for eyeglasses; the word traces to Latin spectare, “look at,” through the idea of things used for seeing.',C('spectacles.s1','vision','He put on his spectacles to read the tiny instructions printed inside the medicine box.','他戴上眼镜，阅读药盒内侧印着的细小说明。','wear/put on spectacles; a pair of spectacles','复数名词指戴在眼前、帮助看清东西的两片镜片和镜框。','The lenses let him focus on small print.','镜片让他看清小字。'),M('He put on his spectacles to read the medicine label, but the word means a public show rather than eyewear.','He put on his spectacles, the lenses that helped him read the medicine label.','在此语境中 put on spectacles 是戴眼镜，不是观看演出。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did he put on his spectacles?','to read tiny print','to watch a rocket launch','to repair the medicine box','Spectacles help him see the small instructions.'),Q(1,'What does spectacles mean here?','eyeglasses','an embarrassing public scene','a type of flower','The plural noun is the ordinary word for eyeglasses.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a pair of spectacles','a spectacle of spectacleses','a pair spectacle','The usual count phrase is “a pair of spectacles.”','collocation'),Q(1,'What is the related singular noun’s older source?','Latin spectaculum, a show or sight','Old English spearwa, a bird','Latin surgere, to rise','Spectacles is linked historically to looking and seeing.','word-formation')]);
P('spectacular','Spectacular is spectacle + -ar, from Latin roots about looking; as an adjective it means strikingly impressive or surprisingly successful, and as a noun it can mean a large public show.',[C('spectacular.s1','scenery','The hikers reached a spectacular overlook just as the sun lit the red cliffs.','徒步者抵达一处壮观的观景点时，夕阳正照亮红色峭壁。','spectacular view/scenery; a spectacular display','形容词表示景象非常壮丽、令人印象深刻。','The view makes a strong visual impression.','景色带来强烈的视觉震撼。'),C('spectacular.s2','results','The small team made a spectacular recovery, winning the final four games after a poor start.','这支小队实现了惊人的反弹，在开局不佳后连赢最后四场。','spectacular success/growth/recovery','形容词也可表示成绩、增长或成功程度惊人。','The unexpected run of wins is unusually successful.','意料之外的连胜成绩十分惊人。'),C('spectacular.s3','entertainment','The city’s summer spectacular combined dancers, projected images, and fireworks in the main square.','这座城市的夏季盛演在主广场融合了舞蹈、投影和焰火。','a television/stage spectacular; mount a spectacular','名词指场面盛大的公开演出或展示。','The event is a large-scale public show.','这场活动是一场大型公开演出。')],M('The team made a spectacular recovery by losing every remaining game and finishing with its worst record.','The team made a spectacular recovery by winning its final four games after a poor start.','连败和最差记录不是令人惊叹的反弹。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What made the overlook spectacular?','the striking view of red cliffs at sunset','the hikers’ ordinary lunch','the small print on a medicine box','Sense 1 is visually impressive.'),Q(2,'Why was the team’s recovery spectacular?','it won four straight games after a poor start','it lost every game','it canceled its season','Sense 2 means surprisingly successful or large.'),Q(3,'What did the city’s summer spectacular include?','dancers, projections, and fireworks','a medical screening test','a single pair of spectacles','As a noun, a spectacular is a large public show.'),Q(2,'Which sentence uses spectacular for results rather than scenery?','Sales made a spectacular jump after the redesign.','The mountain offered a spectacular view.','The square hosted a summer spectacular.','The first describes an unexpectedly large change in results.')]);
})();
